	(30, '2026-06-11 13:30:09.485243+00', 'tejaswini@mimicino.com', 'Product Design & Prototyping Partnership for Mimicino', 'Hello, My name is Tejaswini Kher, and I am one of the founders of Mimicino, a premium pet lifestyle brand currently being developed in India. We are reaching out because we are looking for a product design and development partner who can help us bring our product ideas to life. We have a clear vision for the brand, along with product concepts and references, but are looking for a team that can help translate these ideas into well-designed, manufacturable products and working prototypes. Mimicino is focused on creating thoughtfully designed products for cats and dogs that integrate seamlessly into modern homes. Our goal is to combine aesthetics, functionality, durability, and pet wellbeing while moving away from the traditional look and feel often associated with pet products. At this stage, we are looking for a partner who can support us through the design and development process and help ensure that our products are practical to manufacture and scalable as the brand grows. A brief overview of what we are looking for: Current Stage • Product ideas and concept references • Clear brand vision and target customer • Preliminary research into materials and manufacturing options Product Categories • Pet furniture • Catification products and wall systems • Cat trees and scratchers • Pet beds • Other pet lifestyle and home products Materials We Expect to Work With • Solid wood • Plywood and engineered wood • Metal • Sisal and natural fibres • Upholstery fabrics • Organic fabrics • Banana fibre leather • Biothane • Foam and cushioning materials • Upcycled wood • Upcycled plastic • Other durable, pet-safe materials Support Required • Product design and development • Industrial design and concept refinement • Taking inspiration from our references and ideas and developing distinctive, ownable products that are unique to Mimicino and aligned with our brand vision • CAD drawings and technical specifications • Material recommendations • Engineering for manufacturability • Prototype development and testing • Design refinement based on prototype feedback • Production feasibility and cost optimisation • Development of production-ready documentation and specifications that can be shared with manufacturers for quoting and production We would love to learn more about your experience, process, prototype development capabilities, timelines, pricing structure, and any relevant projects you have worked on in furniture, home products, pet products, or similar categories. If this sounds like a potential fit, we would be happy to schedule a call and share more details about Mimicino and the products we are developing. Looking forward to hearing from you. Best regards, Tejaswini Kher', 'mail sent', 'product-design-inquiry'),
