	(167, '2026-07-08 15:30:15.256251+00', 'prabhukeluskaraarya@gmail.com', 'Application _ Industrial Designer, Aarya Prabhukeluskar, RCA & NID Graduate', 'Respected Iuova Design Company Team,

*I am writing to apply for the Senior Industrial Designer role in Mumbai.*
My name is Aarya Prabhukeluskar, I hold a *Master''s *in Information
Experience Design from the* Royal College of Art, London*, and a
*Bachelor''s* in Industrial Design from the* National Institute of Design.*

I want to be upfront: my professional title to date has been Industrial
Designer, not Senior. But I''d like to make the case for why I believe I can
operate at that level. At *IcarusNova Discovery Pvt. Ltd.* in Bangalore, I
was the *sole tangible product/industrial designer*, which meant I owned
the *entire process *alone, research, concept, CAD, prototyping, client
presentation, and production handoff, across 9-10 concurrent projects
spanning healthcare devices, consumer goods, tech products, packaging as
well as Ui/Ux. I worked directly with engineers, clients, and
manufacturers, and I led and mentored design interns, involving them in
live projects while retaining ownership of final outcomes. That level
of *end-to-end
responsibility,* at a relatively early career stage alongside my master''s
training is what gives me confidence *I can meet the expectations of a
senior-level role*.

My project experience spans exactly the categories you''ve described,
consumer products, medical devices, and connected/wearable technology. I
designed the *Cervicheck* self-swab cervical cancer detection kit that
secured investment on *Shark Tank India*, and a wearable Continuous ECG
monitoring system (Falling in IoT/connected-product exposure) built around
comfort and unobtrusive daily use for home-care patients while problem
solving the original initial prototype. My footwear innovation project, *Ember
01*, incorporated embedded electronics and a live digital feedback
prototype, earning a *provisional patent*. While I have only worked on
Service Design project related to EVs, I bring the same rigorous
form-development and manufacturability thinking that I believe translates
