*Portfolio:*https://www.behance.net/mrugankghogale1', 'mail sent', 'job-application'),
	(163, '2026-07-08 14:00:55.979185+00', 'a.b.chandranath.ballala@gmail.com', 'Applying for the post of senior industrial designer', 'Dear Hiring Manager,

Iuova Design Company

I am an Industrial Designer and Automobile Engineer with over 16 years of
experience spanning product design, automotive styling, manufacturing
engineering, and design strategy. With a Master’s in Industrial Design from
Ramaiah University of Applied Sciences and a foundation built across
leading organisations in the mobility, energy, and social innovation
sectors, I bring a rare blend of creative design thinking and deep
technical fluency to every project I undertake. I am reaching out to
explore opportunities where I can contribute this breadth of experience to
a forward-thinking design team.

My design practice is rooted in human-centred thinking, visual
communication, and a strong command of form. As a Vehicle Stylist at
Igowise Mobility, I developed over 30 design iterations for a narrow-track
three-wheeler — translating 2D concept sketches into refined 3D surface
models using Fusion 360, Autodesk Alias, and producing photorealistic
renders and video visualisations in KeyShot. I have worked extensively on
CMF (Colour, Material, Finish) exploration, brand identity creation, and
ergonomic design. At Volvo Buses India, I designed graphics and colour
schemes for over 200 buses, and created ergonomic production-line
facilities for sleeper coach manufacturing — a formative experience in
balancing aesthetics with real-world manufacturing constraints.

Beyond individual design execution, I am experienced in leading design
projects from concept through to production. At SELCO Foundation, I led
eight design projects for agricultural and micro-enterprise machine tools,
managing cross-functional teams and vendor networks to deliver measurable
improvements in efficiency and cost. At Svitch Moto Corp, I directed a team
of five designers and engineers on an electric motorcycle development
programme, improving team delivery speed and ensuring 100% adherence to
project milestones. This ability to operate at both the conceptual and
strategic levels is something I consider a core part of my value as a
designer.

My technical toolkit includes KeyShot, Fusion 360, Autodesk Alias, Adobe
Creative Suite (Illustrator, Photoshop), Blender and Sketchbook, alongside
a solid grounding in DFM (Design for Manufacturing and Assembly), BOM
engineering, production planning, and material management. I have also
developed and filed a motor patent in India for a two-wheeler EV hybrid
conversion system, reflecting my interest in innovation at the intersection
of design and technology.

My academic work was recognised with the Dr. M.S. Ramaiah Gold Medal for
academic excellence, the Smt. Gowramma Ramaiah Medal for Best PG
Dissertation, and the “Most Innovative Design” award at my thesis
submission. These achievements reflect not just academic rigour, but a
genuine passion for pushing the boundaries of what design can do. I am now
looking to bring this passion and experience to a design studio where bold
ideas, craft, and strategic intent are valued in equal measure.

I would welcome the opportunity to discuss how my background might align
with your team’s needs and current projects. Please find my resume attached
for your consideration.

Warm regards,

Chandranath Ballala

Industrial Designer & Automobile Engineer', 'mail sent', 'job-application'),
