	(175, '2026-07-11 05:00:24.090628+00', 'jpalaskar@gmail.com', 'To develop new dental device system Semi-adjustable Articulator and Facebow system', 'Dear Sir/ Madam

Greetings!

India, as a developing country with a large population of dental students
and practitioners, requires cost-effective alternatives to the expensive
articulators currently available in the market. The high cost of imported
and premium articulator systems often limits their accessibility,
particularly in undergraduate institutions, postgraduate training programs,
and private clinical practice. Consequently, there is a pressing need for
an affordable semi-adjustable articulator that can be widely adopted
without imposing a significant financial burden on users.

However, affordability should not come at the expense of quality or
clinical performance. An ideal articulator for the Indian market should be
robust, precisely engineered, and capable of accurately reproducing
mandibular movements to ensure reliable diagnosis, treatment planning, and
prosthesis fabrication. By combining advanced design features with
economical manufacturing, such an articulator would bridge the gap between
cost and functionality, making high-quality prosthodontic care and
education more accessible while promoting better clinical outcomes.

For transfer of records from patient to articulator a Facebow transfer is
required.

Thanks and regards.

Dr. Jayant N Palaskar

9370015510

