	(177, '2026-07-11 17:31:01.760001+00', 'aishwaryakrishnan169@gmail.com', 'Seeking Guidance on Building a Kids’ Fitness Equipment Brand', 'Dear Vatsal, I hope you’re doing well. Thank you for sharing your email and taking the time to connect with me on LinkedIn. My name is Aishwarya Krishnan. I am a Certified Strength & Conditioning Specialist (CSCS) , a Certified Pre & Postnatal Coach , and the founder of The Strength Squad . I have over 10 years of coaching experience helping individuals build strength and improve performance, and I’m currently also building a prenatal fitness brand, The Bump Squad . Alongside my coaching business, I’m now looking to build a completely new venture in the children’s fitness space. My vision is to design and manufacture high-quality, safe, and durable fitness and strength equipment specifically for children. The goal is to encourage kids to develop strength, coordination, confidence, and a lifelong love for movement through equipment designed exclusively for them. Some of the products I’m envisioning include: • Kids’ barbells and weight plates • Rubber-coated dumbbells and kettlebells • Soft bumper plates • Monkey bars and climbing equipment • Balance and coordination equipment • Other child-safe strength and movement products While I have extensive expertise in fitness coaching, I come from a non-manufacturing background. I’m therefore looking for guidance on how to transform this idea into a successful product-based business. Specifically, I’d love to understand: • The overall product development process from concept to launch • Material selection (EVA, TPE, TPU, EPDM, rubber, etc.) • Industrial design and engineering considerations • Prototyping and product testing • Manufacturing, tooling, and production • Safety standards and certifications for children’s equipment • Finding the right manufacturing partners and suppliers • The complete roadmap to building a scalable brand in this space From what I’ve seen of your experience, I 