Dear Sir/Madam,
I hope this message finds you well.
My name is Anesh Vrindavan, and I represent the Corporate Security team at Amazon. We are issuing this Request for Proposal (RFP) to identify and engage a qualified engineering partner for the design, development, and prototyping of a next-generation automated badge issuance kiosk for deployment across our global corporate offices.
We invite your organization to submit a detailed proposal addressing the scope, requirements, and deliverables outlined below.

  1.  PROJECT OVERVIEW

Amazon Corporate Security seeks to deploy a premium, lightweight, modular badge issuance kiosk that departs from conventional sheet-metal construction. The kiosk will leverage advanced materials such as aluminum honeycomb panels, aircraft-grade aluminum alloys (e.g., 6061-T6, 7075), carbon fiber composites, polycarbonate, and other high-strength lightweight materials as engineering analysis may dictate.
The selected partner will assume full ownership of the product development lifecycle—from concept design through prototype validation and production readiness support.

  1.  SCOPE OF WORK

The proposal must address the following areas:

  *   Complete kiosk structural design from first principles
  *   Material recommendation and sourcing from qualified, certified suppliers
  *   Structural analysis (Finite Element Analysis) and design optimization for strength, stability, and weight reduction
  *   Development of detailed CAD models and manufacturing-ready engineering drawings
  *   Fabrication and validation of a functional prototype
  *   Iterative design refinement and engineering support through production readiness
  *   Documentation including design rationale, material specifications, test reports, and maintenance guides

  1.  DESIGN REQUIREMENTS

  *   Target weight: Approximately 150–200 kg (fully assembled)
  *   Aesthetic standard: Premium industrial design befitting a corporate environment
  *   Modularity: Designed for ease of transportation, rapid assembly, and global deployment
  *   Structural integrity: Capable of supporting users of varying body weights without vibration, deflection, or wobble
  *   Integration readiness: Accommodations for camera systems, badge printer, lighting modules, access control hardware, networking infrastructure, and ancillary electronic components
  *   Serviceability: Removable service panels, accessible internal cable routing, and tool-free maintenance access where feasible
  *   Compliance: Design must conform to applicable safety, ergonomic, and accessibility standards

  1.  PROPOSAL SUBMISSION REQUIREMENTS

Interested vendors are requested to include the following in their proposal:
a) Company profile and organizational overview b) Relevant project experience and case studies (particularly in kiosk engineering, enclosure development, or lightweight structural systems) c) Engineering capabilities, team composition, and key personnel qualifications d) Proposed approach and methodology for this engagement e) Preliminary project timeline with key milestones f) Commercial proposal including cost breakdown by phase (design, prototyping, production support) g) Quality assurance and testing methodology h) References from prior clients for similar engagements

  1.  EVALUATION CRITERIA

Proposals will be evaluated based on:

  *   Demonstrated technical expertise in lightweight structural design and advanced materials
  *   Relevance and quality of prior project experience
  *   Proposed methodology and design approach
  *   Timeline feasibility
  *   Cost competitiveness
  *   Quality of references and client testimonials

  1.  SUBMISSION DETAILS

  *   Submission format: PDF via email
  *   Point of contact: Anesh Vrindavan, Corporate Security, Amazon
  *   Email: avrindav@amazon.com

  1.  TERMS AND CONDITIONS

  *   This RFP does not constitute a commitment to award a contract.
  *   Amazon reserves the right to accept or reject any or all proposals.
  *   All information shared as part of this RFP is confidential and must not be disclosed to third ', 'mail sent', 'product-design-inquiry'),
