	(213, '2026-07-27 16:00:10.710312+00', 'victor.villazon@villazoncode.com', 'Sculptural Ergonomic Body Piece Inquiry // Project RFQ – Villazon Code', 'Dear Iuova Team,




I hope this email finds you well.

I am reaching out on behalf of Villazon Code, a conceptual fashion and luxury brand based in Berlin. We are preparing the development of our flagship statement piece and are seeking an industrial design and engineering partner capable of bridging high-end aesthetics with complex physical engineering.

Why Industrial Product Engineering is Essential for This Project

While the final piece will be executed in high-end metals and gemstones, its unique design places it beyond the scope of traditional jewelry workshops.

The piece is conceived as an articulated snake with a dual purpose:

Wearable Ergonomics: It must drape fluidly, comfortably, and dynamically across the human torso during movement.


Standalone Sculpture: When off the body, it must function as a self-supporting, balanced art sculpture for display.



Balancing gravity, weight distribution, internal mechanics, and structural memory for both states requires dedicated industrial product engineering and kinetic mechanism design rather than standard goldsmithing.

What We Want to Achieve

Kinetic Multi-Link Structure: A modular, articulated metal body designed for fluid movement and structural balance.


Integrated Micro-Mechanics: Embedded internal mechanisms (such as a sound/rattle feature) integrated seamlessly within the cast links.


Luxury Detailing: Precision settings for gemstones and durable, high-spec electroplated finishes.


Concealed Branding: Integrated brand signatures and hallmarking engineered into the inner surfaces of the links for authenticity and IP protection.



What We Need to Achieve It

We are looking for technical support across the following development phases:

3D CAD Engineering & Kinetic Modeling: Translating initial design concepts into precise 3D CAD files (.3DM / .STEP), engineering hidden hinge joints, calculating tolerances, and embedding the internal mechanism.


Prototyping & Physical Validation: Producing 3D-printed SLA/resin prototypes to test ergonomic fit on the body, structural balance off the body, and weight distribution before metal tooling.


Production Management / Tooling Oversight: Overseeing micro-casting (brass/bronze investment casting), link assembly, gem setting, and electroplating (either directly in-house or through your manufacturing network).



Next Steps & Preliminary Inquiry

Before sharing our complete technical pack, initial renders, and design documentation, we require all partners to sign a standard Non-Disclosure Agreement (NDA).

Could you please let us know:

Does your studio handle end-to-end development (Engineering + Prototyping + Managed Production), or do you focus strictly on the Engineering & Prototyping phases?


Could you share your official company details (Registered Name, Tax ID/VAT, Business Address, and Authorized Signatory) so we can issue the NDA for your review?



Once the NDA is signed, we will immediately share the detailed brief for a formal RFQ and timeline estimation.

Looking forward to your response.




Best regards,


Victor Villazon
Brand Director 
Villazon Code
Berlin, Germany', 'mail sent', 'product-design-inquiry'),
	(216, '2026-07-29 09:00:11.172866+00', 'sales02@amisonengineering.com', 'Engineering Design & Simulation Support for Faster Product Development', 'Hello Sir/Madam,
I hope you are doing well.
During product development, engineering teams often face challenges such as multiple design iterations, manufacturability issues, validation failures, and longer development cycles. Identifying and solving these challenges early helps reduce development time, cost, and production risks.
At AMISON Engineering, we support product design organizations as an extended engineering partner by providing design optimization and simulation solutions before manufacturing.
Our capabilities include:
• 3D CAD Modeling & Part Design
• Design Optimization & Design for Manufacturing (DfM)
• Reverse Engineering
• FEA (Structural, Thermal & Fatigue Analysis)
• CFD Simulation for Flow & Thermal Performance
• Rapid Prototyping through Metal & Polymer 3D Printing
• CNC Machining for Functional Components
Whether you are developing new components, improving existing designs, or validating parts before production, our engineering team can help reduce prototype iterations and accelerate the product development cycle.
We would appreciate the opportunity to understand your current engineering challenges and explore how AMISON Engineering can support your upcoming projects.
Looking forward to connecting with you.


Thanks & Regards,
Ashutosh Khodake
Assistant Manager - Business Development
Mob No: +91 7058674513

