	(226, '2026-08-03 08:00:07.156199+00', 'placementcell@iitb.ac.in', 'Invitation to the Placement Season of IIT Bombay 2026-27', 'Dear Hiring Team,

Warm greetings from the Placement Office, Indian Institute of Technology 
Bombay!

I am Rakesh Joshi, Company Coordinator at the Placement Office, IIT 
Bombay, and I''m pleased to formally invite Iuova Design Company to 
participate in the IIT Bombay campus recruitment process for the 2026-27 
placement season.

IIT Bombay has been ranked among the top 3 institutes in India for the 
past 10 years. We are known for our Employer Reputation (scored 
97.8/100) and Engineering and Technology (42nd rank), as per the latest 
QS World University Rankings statistics, making it India''s leading 
technical institute with an acceptance rate of less than 2%.

These metrics underscore the excellence of our academic ecosystem, the 
strength of our research output, and the employability of our graduates.

With over 2400+ graduating students from 17 departments, 3 research 
centers, an Industrial Design Centre School of Design, and 4 
Interdisciplinary Programs, we offer a diverse and deep talent pool. 
Students come from 11 programs, including BTech, BS, BDes, Dual Degree 
(BTech + MTech), MTech, MSc, MS by Research, MA by Research, MPP, MDes, 
and PhD.

Campus Placement Timeline:

  	* Company Registration Opens: _August 2026_
  	* Job Announcement Form (JAF) Opening: _September 2026_
  	* Assessments Begin: _End of September 2026_
  	* Final Interviews: _Begin 1st December 2026_
  	* Joining Date: _June to August 2027_

Recruitment Process Overview:

  	* Register on our Placement Portal:  
https://campus.placements.iitb.ac.in [1]
  	* Receive login credentials upon registration.
  	* Submit the Job Announcement Form (JAF) with job description, salary 
bifurcation, eligibility criteria, etc.
  	* Enter payment details (including GST information) on the Placement 
Portal.
  	* Recruiters need to pay a participation fee of INR 10,000 through the 
Placement portal as a part of the placement process
  	* After the payment confirmation is received from the bank, the 
Placement Office will verify the company''s JAF(s)
  	* The JAF will be opened for students to apply with their resume, 
which can be viewed online by recruiters by logging into our placement 
portal
  	* Conducting technical tests either Online / Offline.
  	* Shortlisting of students by the company.
  	* Final Interviews (on-campus or telephonic/online interview)

Please provide the contact details (phone number and email ID) of a 
point of contact from your team for further communication regarding the 
placement process.

Also, Please find attached the Recruiter Policy document for your 
reference. Kindly go through it carefully and fill out the Customer Code 
Creation Template, then share the completed file with me for further 
processing.

IIT Bombay is committed to inclusive hiring and encourages recruiters to 
adopt PwD-friendly practices during the recruitment process.

We truly appreciate your time and continued support and we look forward 
to a long-lasting collaboration with your esteemed organization.

Please feel free to reach out to me in case you have any queries or need 
further information.

Warm Regards,

Rakesh Joshi
Company Coordinator 2026-27
Placement office, IIT Bombay
Contact: +91 8830744099 | Linkedin [2]

Links:
------
[1] https://campus.placements.iitb.ac.in/
[2] https://www.linkedin.com/in/therakeshjoshi/', 'mail sent', 'job-application'),
