	(266, '2026-08-17 08:30:10.468704+00', 'ravikanttyagi249@gmail.com', 'Key details for Little Buddha', 'Hi Vatsal,

Thank you for sharing your email ID. As discussed, sharing the key details
of Little Buddha below for your reference.

*Q: What are we building?*
*A:* Little Buddha is a premium smart thermal (cold&hot-plunge) and
recovery system for the home and commercial wellness market.

*Q: What stage are we at?*
*A:* We have already developed the initial product concept and defined the
A1/A2 architecture, core technology direction, package space and overall
dimensions.

*Q: What do we need from IUOVA?*
*A:* We need a product development partner to take the existing concept
from MVP to a premium, production-ready product, rather than developing a
completely new architecture.

*Q: What would IUOVA''s scope include?*
*A:* Industrial design, product refinement, mechanical engineering/CAD,
component integration, DFM/DFA, engineering drawings, prototyping support,
testing/iteration and manufacturing readiness.

*Q: What about manufacturing?*
*A:* We will work with specialized partners for refrigeration,
rotomoulding, acrylic and other manufacturing requirements. We expect IUOVA
to coordinate with these partners and resolve design/engineering issues
during development.

*Q: What is the expected end point?*
*A:* A prototype. We want to reach *5–10 production-intent units*, which
can be deployed in gyms/pilot locations and/or sold to initial customers
for real-world validation.

*Q: What are the key deliverables?*
*A:* Final industrial design, production-ready CAD, engineering drawings,
CMF, DFM/DFA, prototype development and testing support, and a
manufacturing-ready product package.

*Q: What is the long-term objective?*
*A:* To build a premium, globally competitive smart recovery product and
establish a scalable product platform for future Little Buddha variants.

Please let us know if you need any additional information or reference
material to prepare the proposal.

Regards,
Ravikant Tyagi
Founder, Little Buddha', 'mail sent', 'product-design-inquiry'),
