	(282, '2026-08-23 13:00:09.342984+00', 'blissfood@gmail.com', 'Product Development Enquiry – Indian Chai Cooking Appliance', 'Hi,

I’m Chef Amninder Sandhu, a chef and restaurateur based in Mumbai, and the founder of several restaurant concepts including Kikli, Bawri and Barbet & Pals. My cooking is deeply rooted in Indian regional food traditions, and a large part of my work involves taking traditional techniques and ingredients and translating them into a contemporary context.

I’m currently developing a product that I’m quite excited about and am looking for the right product design and engineering partner to help bring it to life.

The concept is a beautiful countertop chai pot designed specifically to cook Indian chai, rather than simply boil water or steep tea.

The idea is to have a vessel with concealed heating and a programmable timer/temperature cycle that allows you to actually cook the chai — including boiling and simmering milk, tea and whole spices. The finished chai would then be poured through an integrated fine stainless-steel sieve built into the mouth of the spout, so that loose tea leaves, ginger and whole spices are strained as you pour.

I want the product to feel like a beautiful Indian object that can sit on a dining table, rather than looking like a conventional electric kettle or kitchen appliance.

At this stage, I am looking for a partner who can help with feasibility, industrial design, thermal/heating engineering, mechanical engineering, electronics and development of the first functional prototype.

I would like to begin with a functional prototype and, once the cooking process and mechanism are proven, develop the industrial design and eventually take it into manufacturing.

I’d love to know if this is within your scope and whether we could set up a meeting to discuss the concept.

Warm regards,
Chef Amninder Sandhu
Founder / Chef
Kikli | Bawri | Barbet & Pals', 'mail sent', 'product-design-inquiry'),
