	(304, '2026-09-02 00:00:10.245845+00', 'pkim@pmkincorporated.com', 'Inquiry – Industrial Design & Product Development Partnership', 'Dear IUOVA Team,

My name is Paul Kim, and I am contacting you on behalf of PMK Supply, Inc.,
a U.S.-based company.

We are currently developing a new consumer product in the desk organization
and cable management category and are looking for an industrial design and
product development partner.

In addition to this project, we have several other consumer product
concepts that we plan to develop over time. Rather than engaging a design
firm for only a single project, we are interested in establishing a
long-term relationship with a capable and cost-effective product
development team.

We are currently exploring product development partners in India because we
believe India may offer a strong combination of industrial design,
engineering capability, manufacturing knowledge, and competitive
development costs for an ongoing product development partnership.

The general concept for our current project is a modular desk cable
management system designed to organize charging and power cables while
keeping the workspace clean and uncluttered.

The product may incorporate a combination of:

   - A desk-mounted or under-desk base system
   - Organized cable storage and management
   - Mechanical cable retraction or controlled cable extension
   - Modular/removable components
   - Accessory storage for power adapters, chargers, or related items
   - Simple installation suitable for consumer use

Our objective is not simply to redesign an existing cable organizer. We
would like to develop a well-integrated, differentiated consumer product
with strong usability, clean industrial design, and practical
manufacturability.

We are looking for a partner who can potentially provide:

   1. Industrial design and concept development
   2. Mechanical design and engineering
   3. Mechanism development where required
   4. 3D CAD and production-ready engineering files
   5. Prototype development and testing
   6. DFM and manufacturing support

At this initial stage, we would first like to determine whether this type
of project fits your team''s experience and capabilities.

If so, could you please provide:

   - Examples of similar non-electronic consumer products or mechanical
   products your team has developed
   - Your typical product development process
   - Which of the above services you can provide in-house
   - An approximate budget range for a project of this nature
   - Typical development timeline
   - Whether you can work under an NDA before we share detailed concepts,
   drawings, and product requirements

We are currently evaluating several product development firms and would be
happy to provide more detailed information after determining the
appropriate development partner.

Thank you, and I look forward to hearing from you.

Best regards,

Paul Kim
PMK Supply, Inc.

-- 
Paul Kim
CEO

