	(350, '2026-09-14 07:30:09.516733+00', 'monika@getqorel.com', 'Industrial Design & Mechanical Engineering Project – Premium Consumer Hardware', 'Hello,

I am the founder of QOREL, a consumer product startup currently developing
a premium portable fine mist product.

We are looking for an industrial design and mechanical engineering partner
to take the product from its current concept stage through functional
prototyping and towards manufacturing-ready design.

The product is a compact refillable consumer device built around an
existing bottle, pump and actuator system, which has already been selected
and will remain unchanged. The new hardware therefore needs to be designed
around and fully compatible with these existing components.

The development scope would include:

   - Industrial design and refinement of the overall product form,
   proportions and premium aesthetic
   - Integration of a keychain / attachment element as an essential part of
   the product design
   - Mechanical integration of the existing bottle, pump and actuator
   system into the new hardware
   - Development of the user interaction / activation mechanism around the
   existing actuator
   - Protection against accidental activation while the product is being
   carried
   - Secure retention and easy replacement of the bottle/refill
   - Mechanical engineering of the complete assembly
   - Material and manufacturing process selection
   - Functional prototyping and design iterations
   - DFM and preparation of manufacturing-ready CAD and technical
   documentation
   -

Our current material direction is an anodized aluminium outer body,
stainless steel visible keychain hardware and appropriate high-load/wear
components, with engineering polymers used for suitable internal functional
components. However, we are open to engineering recommendations based on
manufacturability, durability and cost.

We already have physical samples and technical drawings of the existing
bottle, pump and actuator system, which can be provided for the engineering
process.

Before sharing more detailed product information, I would like to
understand whether this type of project fits your capabilities. Further
product details can be shared after an NDA is in place.

Could you please provide:

   - 2–3 examples of similar consumer hardware products you have developed,
   particularly products involving mechanical interaction, small mechanisms
   and metal/plastic assemblies.
   - Which stages your team handled in those projects (industrial design,
   mechanical engineering, mechanism development, prototyping, DFM, production
   support).
   - Whether your team has experience developing hardware around existing
   off-the-shelf components that must remain unchanged.
   - Whether your team has experience designing products combining anodized
   aluminium, stainless steel and engineering plastics.
   - Your typical development process from concept through functional
   prototype and manufacturing-ready CAD.
   - An indicative timeline and budget range for a project of this scope.
   - Confirmation that all final CAD/source files, technical documentation
   and intellectual property developed specifically for the project can be
   fully owned by QOREL and transferred to any manufacturer selected by us.
   -

We already have the existing bottle, pump and actuator samples, technical
drawings, defined product requirements and an established overall product
direction, so the project would not be starting from an initial idea stage.

If the project is within your scope, I would be happy to arrange a short
introductory call. Further technical and product-specific information can
then be shared under NDA.

Best regards,

Monika Litvinaitė
Founder

