	(387, '2026-09-21 20:30:08.008399+00', 'force24sa@gmail.com', 'Enquiry – Product Engineering & Development of Force24 Premium Extension Board', 'Dear Team,


We are looking for a product engineering and development partner for a new premium electrical extension board that we plan to launch in the Indian market under our Force24brand.


We have already developed the initial product concept and industrial-design direction. The concept render is attached for reference.


Please note that the attached render represents our intended design language, appearance and product positioning only. It is not an engineering or manufacturing drawing. Internal construction, dimensions and technical specifications are to be finalized during engineering development.


Our initial product concept is:


  *   5 AC sockets
  *   Single master power switch
  *   Child-safety shutters
  *   Overload protection
  *   Surge protection, subject to engineering feasibility
  *   Approximately 2-metre power cable
  *   Flame-retardant engineering-grade enclosure
  *   Premium off-white upper housing with translucent crimson-red lower housing
  *   Stable anti-slip base
  *   Compact, premium form factor with an inclined socket surface
  *   No USB charging ports
  *   No individual switches for each socket


The GM 3060 extension board may be considered as a general market benchmark for functionality and usability; however, we do not intend to copy its product design or construction. Our Force24 concept and design language should remain distinctive.


We are looking for an experienced engineering partner who can convert our concept into a safe, reliable, manufacturable and mass-production-ready product while retaining the overall Force24 exterior design direction.


We require support for:


  *   Electrical architecture and internal layout
  *   Socket contact and busbar engineering
  *   Master switch and overload-protection system
  *   Surge-protection engineering, if incorporated
  *   Child-safety shutter mechanism
  *   Cable, plug, termination and strain-relief engineering
  *   Mechanical/enclosure engineering
  *   Internal insulation, barriers and clearances
  *   Material selection
  *   Thermal and electrical safety considerations
  *   3D CAD and detailed engineering drawings
  *   Functional prototype development
  *   Engineering testing and validation
  *   Design for Manufacturing (DFM)
  *   Final BOM
  *   Production-ready drawings and technical documentation
  *   Tooling/mould-development support


The product should be engineered using appropriate safety practices and suitable materials so that subsequent compliance testing can be undertaken without requiring fundamental product redesign.


We would prefer the project quotation to be divided into the following stages:


1. Feasibility & Engineering Architecture

2. Detailed Electrical & Mechanical Engineering

3. Functional Prototype & Engineering Validation

4. DFM & Production-Ready Documentation

5. Tooling / Mould Development Support – quoted separately


Please also share examples of any 230V consumer electrical products your team has previously engineered, particularly extension boards, power strips, sockets, switches, plugs or similar electrical accessories.


At this stage, we are developing only the Force24 extension board.


Kindly share your proposed development approach, scope of deliverables, estimated timeline and commercial quotation.


Regards,

Sharif Khan

Force24 Lifestyle Pvt. Ltd.', 'mail sent', 'product-design-inquiry'),
