	(410, '2026-09-28 23:01:29.178805+00', 'nutan_pandit@yahoo.com', 'Inquiry – Consumer Product Engineering & Prototyping', 'Hello iUOVA,
I’m a US-based entrepreneur in the early stages of developing a new consumer kitchen appliance and am exploring engineering design and prototyping partners in India. I came across your company and would like to learn more about your capabilities and how you typically work with early-stage founders.
I’d particularly like to understand:
• What services do you provide across product development — concept engineering, mechanical/electromechanical design, electronics, CAD, industrial design, prototyping, testing and manufacturing support?
• Do you work with international clients, particularly US-based clients? If so, how do you typically structure the engagement and collaboration?
• Do you work with individual entrepreneurs and early-stage startups, or primarily with established companies?
• Can you share examples of consumer products you have developed, particularly kitchen appliances or other electromechanical products?
• How do you typically structure your fees — hourly, fixed-price, or milestone-based? What would be a typical range for taking an early-stage concept through a functional prototype?
• How do you source components and parts for prototypes? If a required component is not readily available in India, how do you handle sourcing?
• Do you have in-house prototyping capabilities, or do you work with external fabrication/prototyping partners?
• Can you support the transition from a working prototype to design-for-manufacturing (DFM) and eventually production?
• How do you protect a client’s confidential product concept and intellectual property? Are you comfortable signing an NDA before detailed product information is shared?
• Who owns the designs, CAD files, technical documentation and any IP developed during the engagement?

If your capabilities are a good fit, I’d be happy to schedule a brief introductory conversation and share more about the product.
Best regards,Nutan Pandit', 'mail sent', 'product-design-inquiry'),
	(402, '2026-09-26 07:30:19.708971+00', 'official.kennethsterlin@gmail.com', 'Product Design & Engineering Enquiry | Modular Food-Container System', 'Dear IUOVA Team,

I am an India-based founder developing a proprietary modular food-container
system and am currently evaluating a product design and engineering partner
to take the product from its current concept stage through to manufacturing
readiness.

The core product architecture is already established, and I have an initial
physical prototype. The next stage requires a combination of industrial
design and mechanical engineering, including refinement of the product
architecture, sealing and latching mechanisms, tolerance engineering,
functional prototyping, DFM and manufacturing-ready CAD.

The Premium version of the system combines double-wall vacuum
stainless-steel food modules with injection-moulded bases and lids,
silicone seals, mechanical latching and stacking interfaces, and multiple
interchangeable module sizes working within one common platform.

My intention is to manufacture in China, so I am looking for a design
partner who can not only develop the product technically, but also support
the transition into tooling and work with the selected manufacturer during
DFM and handover.

The project contains non-public product architecture and mechanical
details, so I would prefer to have an NDA in place before sharing the
detailed technical brief, CAD and prototype information.

If this is within IUOVA''s scope, I would be interested in discussing your
approach to a programme of this nature, relevant experience with
mechanically complex consumer products, and how you would typically
structure and price the engagement.

Best regards,

*Kenneth Sterlin*
