	('6b01ae31-bd91-45e8-96a2-74a625b60eaa', 'Georgina Casey', 'g.casey2788@hotmail.com', '+353852870834', 'NA', 'Start up business ', 'Keepsakes ', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'First product to be developed is a dog egg cup and spoon ', '{"Product Design Services (Industrial Design)","Prototyping Services"}', 'TBC ', '1 - 2 months', 'Slot for spoon to fit and The design must be elegant, minimalist, safe for children, durable, corrosion-resistant and manufacturable at scale. ', false, NULL, false, false, NULL, 'Have you previously designed consumer products, premium gifts, keepsakes, homeware or decorative metal products that progressed to commercial manufacture and retail sale? If so, please provide examples and explain your process from concept through manufacturing.', 4, 'Google', '2026-06-22', '01:00 PM', '["https://oscdtdlwdrwvjvteqcix.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/video%20and%20image/1782049945295-ga54c.jpeg","https://oscdtdlwdrwvjvteqcix.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/video%20and%20image/1782049945298-lzvjt.jpeg"]', '2026-06-21 13:52:26.953+00', '[{"id":"reply-reminder-1782099005095","to":"g.casey2788@hotmail.com","cc":["developer@iuova.in","info@iuova.in","support@iuova.in"],"subject":"Reminder: IUOVA Meeting on Monday, June 22, 2026 at 01:00 PM (Asia/Kolkata) - today","body":"Hi Georgina Casey,\n\nThis is a reminder that your meeting is today.\n\nDate: Monday, June 22, 2026\nTime: 01:00 PM (Asia/Kolkata)\nMeeting link: https://meet.google.com/dtk-bczw-nyd\n\nIf you need to reschedule, just reply to this email.\n\nRegards,\nIUOVA Team","sentAt":"2026-06-22T03:30:05.095Z","status":"sent","templateId":"meeting-reminder-today","messageIdHeader":"<1fea28d7-1c25-1e2c-25ed-fbe38510feb7@iuova.in>","references_id":"<d6572905-d65b-c18e-3dd1-ef62b4f5516c@iuova.in> <4ffba49e-18f2-5a2f-eb77-ed218a16e078@iuova.in>","gmailThreadId":null,"direction":"outbound","source":"smtp"}]', 'https://meet.google.com/dtk-bczw-nyd', NULL, '<4ffba49e-18f2-5a2f-eb77-ed218a16e078@iuova.in>', '<d6572905-d65b-c18e-3dd1-ef62b4f5516c@iuova.in>', false, false, NULL, 'Stainless steel keepsakes ', false, NULL, NULL),
	('96fe225f-98b3-468d-abae-2e35e19082eb', 'Eshaan Mehta', 'eshaan@mersiv.in', '9819918315', 'Mersiv Labs LLP', 'Not up yet', 'Mersiv Labs LLP designs and sells an AI physical desk pet robot called Blob that pairs with a companion mobile application. Blob is fully conversational in English, with planned support for additional languages, and is built for everyday companionship, learning assistance, and productivity for users aged 13 and above. ', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'Blob is an AI physical desk pet built on an off-the-shelf hardware platform with a custom personality, memory, and behaviour layer designed from the ground up to feel and behave like a living creature. The hardware BOM, cloud backend, companion app and firmware are close to production readiness.

Scope of work for this engagement:

1) Industrial design of the Blob enclosure — a creature-first form factor that houses the existing electronics (ESP32-S3 audio board, 1.47" IPS LCD, three capacitive touch sensors, speaker, microphones, LiPo battery, USB-C port) while reading and feeling like a small living companion, not a gadget.

2) Visor/face panel design — a tinted transparent panel sitting over the LCD so the display edges disappear and animated eyes appear to float in a dark, character-like face. Includes material selection, tint level, curvature, and integration with the opaque shell.

3) Touch sensor integration — placement and shell curvature design for three capacitive touch zones (head, left, right) that invite natural petting and poking, not button-pressing.

4)CMF (color, material, finish) direction supporting the living-creature feel.

5)Product engineering / CAD-for-manufacturing — production-aware CAD output, DFMA-aware design choices. 

6) Prototyping — at least one fully-assembled, hand-held physical prototype suitable for demos, user feedback, and investor conversations.', '{"Product Engineering Services","Prototyping Services","Product Design Services (Industrial Design)"}', '5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)', '1 - 2 months', 'Blob must read and feel like a small living creature, not an electronic gadget. The non-negotiable design elements are:

1) Seamless visor effect over the display — a 1.47" IPS color LCD (ST7789V3, 320×172) sits behind a tinted/smoked transparent panel so the screen edges disappear and animated eyes appear to float in a dark, character-like face. Reference: how Anki Vector and Cozmo execute their faces. This is the single most important aesthetic element.

2) Creature-first form factor — spherical/rounded character form that invites being held and touched, not a device silhouette.

3) Touch-friendly shell integration — three capacitive touch zones (head, left, right) housed in the shell so they invite natural petting and poking gestures, not button presses. Sensor placement and shell curvature must complement each other.

4) Clean component housing — the enclosure must cleanly house the existing electronics (ESP32-S3 audio board, 1.47" LCD, three capacitive touch sensors, speaker, microphones, LiPo battery, USB-C port) with proper sound channeling for speaker and mic clarity.

5) CMF direction — material, color, and finish recommendations that support the living-creature feel, especially the visor material and tint level, tested against the actual LCD brightness.

6) Production-aware CAD output — final CAD files suitable for a small-batch prototype run ', true, 'Mentioned in the design brief', false, false, 'To be discussed', 'We are an early-stage, solo-founder hardware company based in Mumbai. Blob is our first product, pre-launch and pre-revenue. Open to creative engagement structures (reduced upfront fee with per-unit royalty, milestone-based payments) if of interest.

Current state: working firmware, cloud pipeline, expression and personality engine, sourced hardware on a development board. What''s missing is the body. V1 needs to prove Blob can exist as a presentable, hand-held, functioning physical product — for user testing, demos, and investor conversations. 

What would help us evaluate fit: any character-driven or expressive industrial design work in your portfolio, your typical engagement structure for early-stage startups, and experience with displays behind tinted panels and integrated capacitive touch sensors.', 3, 'Google', '2026-06-22', '05:00 PM', '["https://oscdtdlwdrwvjvteqcix.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/video%20and%20image/1781776677600-3gigv7.pdf"]', '2026-06-18 09:57:59.892+00', '[{"id":"reply-tc-client-19efc996188f11e7","to":"support@iuova.in","cc":[],"subject":"Re: Techno - Commercial offer update follow up","body":"Hello Team IUOVA, \r\n\r\nThank you for sending the offer so promptly. \r\n\r\nPlease allow me some time to evaluate it. Will reach out with a meeting request \r\n\r\n\r\nBest,\r\nEshaan\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEshaan Mehta\r\n\r\nCEO & Founder, Mersiv\r\nEmail: mailto:eshaan@mersiv.in?subject=Hello \r\nTel:+91 9819918315\r\nAddress: Crescent Bay, Jerbai Wadia Road, Bhoiwada Parel, Mumbai,Maharashtra, India - 400012\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nFrom:  < mailto:support@iuova.in >\r\nTo: < mailto:eshaan@mersiv.in >\r\nCc: < mailto:support@iuova.in >, < mailto:crm@iuova.in >, < mailto:info@iuova.in >\r\nDate: Wed, 24 Jun 2026 09:00:16 +0530\r\nSubject: Techno - Commercial offer update follow up\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nHi Eshaan Mehta,\r\n\r\nGreetings to you!\r\n\r\nJust checking in to see if you had a chance to review our Techno Commercial offer in detail.\r\n\r\nWe can arrange a quick 15 minutes meeting to explain in detail if required.\r\n\r\nIf you have any questions, please reply to this email.\r\n\r\nWe are happy to help.\r\n\r\nAwaiting your positive response!\r\n\r\n>Regards,\r\n\r\nRegards,\r\nIUOVA Team","sentAt":"2026-06-25T02:25:39.000Z","status":"read","templateId":null,"