	('18608d6d-e194-49dd-b4ce-4ac64f516583', 'Amruta Nikte', 'amrutanikte@gmail.com', '16477640671', 'RedCup', 'n/a', 'Reusable Red Cup (Party cup) circular system', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT BRIEF
Reusable Red Party Cup
Written by: Amruta Nikte
1.	Project Overview
Development of a durable, reusable plastic party cup inspired by the classic red disposable Solo-style cup.
The objective is to create a reusable alternative that provides a similar user experience to a conventional red disposable party cup, minimizing behavioural friction and making the transition to reusable cups easy.
The initial project will involve developing 2–3 functional prototypes for usability and material evaluation. One prototype/design will subsequently be selected for a small production run for an initial rental pilot.

2.	 Product Concept
Product: Reusable red party cup
Primary use: Cold beverages at house parties, college events, outdoor gatherings and similar occasions.
The product should:
•	Replicate the overall look, feel and drinking experience of a classic red disposable party cup.
•	Feel as similar as reasonably possible to a disposable cup while providing substantially greater durability.
•	Be lightweight and comfortable to hold.
•	Be durable enough for repeated commercial/recreational use.
•	Be stackable for storage and transportation.
•	Have a bright/glossy red appearance.
•	Maintain the familiar tapered party-cup shape and proportions.
•	Machine wash safe for at least 200 cycles
•	Should not leave any smell or residue of drinks consumed previously

3. Reference Product / Dimensions
The reference product is the 18 oz red Solo party cup, one of the most recognizable party cups used for house parties and events.
Reference specifications:
•	Capacity: 18 US fl oz / approximately 532 mL
•	Height: approximately 4.71 in / 120 mm
•	Maximum top width/diameter: approximately 3.88 in / 99 mm
The reusable product should maintain approximately the same external dimensions and capacity, subject to engineering recommendations.
The goal is not to copy the proprietary design, but to replicate the familiar user experience and general form factor while creating an independently designed reusable product.

4. Material Requirements
Highest priority: food-contact safety for the Canadian market.
The material and manufacturing process must be suitable for repeated contact with beverages and comply with applicable Canadian food-contact requirements.
Health Canada''s framework requires food-contact materials not to impart harmful substances to food; the manufacturer is responsible for ensuring suitability for the intended use.
Please recommend:
•	Appropriate food-contact-compliant plastic/material
•	Suitable colourants/additives for the red colour
•	Appropriate manufacturing process
•	Any required material documentation, testing or certification
•	Whether virgin or recycled material is appropriate for this application
Material selection should prioritize:
1.	Food-contact safety
2.	Dishwasher/machine-wash durability
3.	Mechanical durability
4.	Low weight
5.	Cost-effective scalable manufacturing
6.	End-of-life recyclability, where practical

5. Performance Requirements
The cup should:
•	Be dishwasher/machine washable.
•	Withstand a minimum target of 200 dishwasher cycles without cracking, warping, disintegrating or becoming unsuitable for use.
•	Maintain structural integrity during normal handling.
•	Resist cracking or breaking when dropped under normal party/event conditions.
•	Not feel excessively flexible or flimsy.
•	Not be excessively heavy compared with the disposable reference cup.
•	Remain comfortable to hold and drink from.
•	Maintain its shape and food- contact compliant after repeated washing.
•	Maintain acceptable appearance after repeated washing.
Note: Please advise whether the 200-cycle requirement is technically appropriate and recommend an appropriate test protocol for validation.

6. Prototype Scope
Develop 2–3 functional prototypes, preferably using the intended or a technically representative production material/process rather than a purely visual 3D-printed model.
The prototypes should allow evaluation of:
•	Drinking experience
•	Grip and comfort
•	Flexibility/rigidity
•	Weight
•	Durability
•	Dishwasher performance
•	Material suitability
•	Overall similarity to the disposable reference cup
Please advise on the most cost-effective prototyping method that can produce a genuinely functional prototype while providing meaningful information about the eventual production material and manufacturing process.
', '{"Prototyping Services"}', '5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)', '2 - 3 months', 'PRODUCT DEVELOPMENT BRIEF
