-
Timer: 2h / 4h / 8h settings via App/Touch
Air Quality feedback: PM2.5 Value 
3-Color LED Ring (Green/Orange/Red) for AQI


Technical Specifications

Power input (Voltage) - 220-240V AC (Device Input: 24V DC)
Rated Power- 40W (Max)
Amount of Perticulate Clean Air (CADR) - 280 - 320 m3/hr

UV LED: Yes
Applicable Area - Up to 350-400 sq. ft.
Noise (High Speed)- 52 dB
Noise (Low Speed)- 30 dB
Filter Layers: 3 Layers (Fabric Pre-filter, H13 HEPA, Active Carbon)
Recommended Filter Change: Yes
Air Quality Sensors: PM2.5', true, 'We will be developing Mobile based App and Firmware', false, true, '5000', 'REQUEST FOR PROPOSAL (RFP) – ENGINEERING DESIGN & PROTOTYPE DEVELOPMENT
TO: Design & Engineering Consultancies / Product Development Firms
FROM: PARK Innovations Pvt. Ltd.
PROJECT: PAR-400 Residential Air Purifier – Concept to Investment-Ready Prototype
DATE: January 30, 2026

1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY
PARK Innovations seeks a qualified engineering design partner to develop the PAR-400, a residential air purifier targeting the Indian and outside market. The objective is to deliver 5 functional EVT (Engineering Verification Test) units suitable for investor demonstrations, regulatory pre-compliance testing, and field trials.
This is not a conceptual industrial design exercise. We require a manufacturing-ready engineering package that proves the product can be mass-produced within strict cost targets (BOM ₹5,500–7,500 at 5k volume) while meeting performance benchmarks (CADR 300 m³/h, Noise <51 dB(A)).
Your Scope: Complete mechanical, electrical, and firmware engineering; soft-tooling for representative parts; assembly of 2 working prototypes; validation testing documentation.

2. SCOPE OF WORK (PHASED DELIVERABLES)

Phase 1: Engineering Design & Analysis
Objective: Frozen CAD and engineering documentation ready for prototyping.
Deliverables Required:
Industrial Design Refinement: Finalize CMF (Color-Material-Finish) for investor presentation; ergonomics validation for Indian households (floor/desktop dual use).
Mechanical Engineering:
Complete 3D CAD (SolidWorks/CREO, native files + STEP), fully manufacturable using injection molding and sheet metal.
2D manufacturing drawings (GD&T per ISO 1101) for all custom parts.
Tolerance stack-up analysis (critical: filter sealing, fan balance, PCB fit).
Structural FEA: Drop test simulation (ISTA 2A standard), vibration analysis for shipping.
Electrical Engineering:
Schematic capture (Altium/OrCAD) and PCB Layout (2-layer, SMT,single-sided load).
BOM selection for all electronic components
Firmware architecture: Sensor fusion (PM2.5 + optional TVOC), motor PID control, touch HMI, error handling.
Airflow Engineering: CFD analysis of fan volute and filter housing; pressure drop verification; acoustic simulation (frequency response prediction).

Phase 2: Design for Manufacturing (DFM) & Soft Tooling 
Objective: Bridge tooling for prototype parts that represent final production quality.
Deliverables Required:
DFM Reports: Mold flow analysis for ABS housings; draft angle verification; sink mark prediction.
Soft Tooling Production:
Aluminum/Silicone bridge molds for housing components (2 sets: upper/lower).
Forming tools for sheet metal grille components.
Low-volume injection molding of 10 sets of parts (allowing for 2 assemblies + spares).
First Article Inspection (FAI): Dimension reports for molded parts against 2D drawings.

Phase 3: EVT Prototype Assembly
Objective: 2 fully functional, investor-presentable units.
Deliverables Required:
PCB Assembly: Populated and tested circuit boards (ICT/Boundary scan).
Mechanical Integration: Full assembly of 2 units using soft-tooled parts and off-the-shelf components (fans, sensors).
Calibration: PM2.5 sensor calibration against reference instrument; fan curve mapping; noise measurement.
Test Reports:
Performance: CADR testing per ANSI/AHAM AC-1 protocol (smoke/turbidity method).
Safety: Dielectric strength, leakage current, temperature rise (pre-compliance to IS 13252).
Reliability: 500-hour continuous run test on 2 units.

Phase 4: Design Validation & Documentation (Weeks 14-16)
Objective: Package suitable for investor due diligence and factory handover.
Deliverables Required:
Design History File (DHF): Complete engineering change log, calculation notebooks, test data.
Manufacturing Transfer Package: Production-ready drawings, suggested supplier list (SSPL), assembly instructions (SOPs).
Investor Presentation Support: High-quality renderings, exploded views, cost analysis validation, competitive benchmarking report.

3. TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS (MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS)
3.1 Performance Targets

Test Method: CADR (Smoke) ≥280 m³/h ANSI/AHAM AC-1
Coverage Area: 350–400 sq ft @ 4.8 ACH
Calculated from CADR
Noise Level
≤55 dB(A) @ Turbo (1m); ≤32 dB(A) @ Sleep
IEC 60704-2-1
Power Consumption
≤40W (Turbo); ≤5W (Sleep)
Power meter
Filter Life
6 months (HEPA); 12 months (Carbon)
Calculated based on usage model

3.2 Cost Constraints (Critical)
Target BOM Cost: INR 5,500–7,000 per unit at 10,000 MOQ (current pricing).
Design to Cost: All component selections must have identified suppliers with quoted pricing; no "gold plating" or over-specification.
Manufacturing Processes: Restricted to high-volume capable methods:
Injection molding (thermoplastics: ABS, PC/ABS, PA6-GF)
Sheet metal stamping (galvanized steel, aluminum)
PCB SMT/THT
Ultrasonic welding (filter sealing)

3.3 Regulatory & Safety
Primary: IS 13252 (Information Technology Equipment Safety - harmonized with IEC 60950/62368)
EMC: CISPR 32 Class B (residential) pre-compliance
RoHS: All materials must be RoHS 3 compliant for future export capability

3.4 Design Specifics
Form Factor: Vertical tower, max height 650mm, footprint ≤250×250mm
Airflow: Bottom 360° intake → Pre-filter → HEPA H13 → Activated Carbon → Top discharge
Controls: Capacitive touch (3 speeds + Auto), PM2.5 LED indicator ring (traffic light colors), Filter reset button
Power: 220-240V AC, 50Hz, internal SMPS (universal input 100-240V preferred if cost-neutral)

4. DELIVERABLES CHECKLIST FOR FINAL HANDOVER
Your firm must provide the following at project completion:
Engineering Data
[ ] Native CAD files (SolidWorks 2022 or CREO 8.0 compatible)
[ ] Complete 2D drawing package (PDF + DWG) with GD&T
[ ] PCB design files (Gerbers, drill files, pick-and-place files)
[ ] Firmware source code (commented, with build instructions)
[ ] Bill of Materials (BOM): Master BOM and EBOM (Engineering BOM) with manufacturer part numbers and supplier contacts
Prototypes
[ ] 2× fully functional EVT units ( aesthetically finished, "investor-ready" appearance)
[ ] 1× "engineering mule" (transparent/translucent housing for airflow visualization, if possible)
[ ] Spare components kit (1 extra fan assemblies, 2 extra PCBs, 2 extra filter sets)
Documentation
[ ] DFMEA (Design Failure Mode Effects Analysis)
[ ] Test Reports: CADR validation, Noise measurement, Safety pre-compliance, Thermal imaging
[ ] Assembly Instructions: Illustrated SOPs suitable for semi-skilled Indian labor
[ ] Service Manual: Troubleshooting guide, filter replacement procedure, calibration protocol
[ ] Cost Analysis Report: Validated BOM costing with 3 quotes per critical component (fan, sensor, filters)
IP & Legal
[ ] Invention Disclosure: List of any patentable innovations discovered during development (ownership: PARK Innovations)
[ ] Design Rights: Assignment of all industrial design rights to PARK Innovations
[ ] Third-Party IP Clearance: Confirmation that no open-source contamination (GPL/copyleft) exists in firmware without disclosure

5. PROJECT TIMELINE
Approximate Duration: 16 weeks from kickoff to final delivery
Key Milestones:
Week 2: Design Review 1 (Architecture frozen)
Week 4: Critical Design Review (CDR) – CAD complete, PCB layout released
Week 9: First Parts Ready (FAI acceptable)
Week 12: Alpha Build (power-on, basic function)
Week 14: Beta Build (5 units complete, testing started)
Week 16: Final Delivery (documentation + prototypes)


6. INVESTOR-READINESS REQUIREMENTS
Since these prototypes will be used for Series A fundraising, specific attention must be paid to:
Aesthetic Quality: Soft-tooled parts must achieve 90% of final production surface finish (no visible layer lines, proper texture)
Demo Reliability: Units must survive 20+ demonstrations without failure (robust cable management, strain relief)
Data Package: Prepare a "Technical Investment Memorandum" summarizing:
Competitive teardown analysis (vs. Xiaomi, Honeywell, Dyson)
Manufacturing margin analysis (COGS vs. retail price)
Scalability assessment (supplier capacity, tooling investment required for 100k units)
Patent Support: Provide technical descriptions and sketches for any novel features (sealing mechanisms, airflow paths) to support provisional patent filings.

7. COMMERCIAL TERMS & EVALUATION CRITERIA
Budget Expectation
Budget Range: ₹18,00,000 – ₹25,00,000 (all-inclusive: engineering, soft tooling, 5 prototypes, testing)
Payment Terms: 30% kickoff, 30% CDR, 20% First Build, 20% Final Delivery
Currency: INR; Taxes as applicable (GST)
Evaluation Criteria (Weightage)
Technical Capability (40%): Demonstrated experience in HVAC, consumer appliances, or mechatronic products
Speed to Market (25%): Realistic schedule with buffer management
Cost Engineering (20%): Evidence of prior DTC (Design to Cost) success in consumer electronics
Geographic Presence (15%): Preference for firms with presence in India (Delhi NCR, Bangalore, or Mumbai) for ease of collaboration; however, global firms with Indian partners accepted
Submission Requirements
Please submit your proposal including:
Technical Approach: Methodology for Phase 1-4, team structure, software tools
Portfolio: Relevant case studies (2-3 consumer appliances or similar complexity)
Detailed Cost Breakdown: Engineering hours, tooling costs, prototype materials, project management
Risk Register: Your assessment of top 3 technical risks and mitigation strategies
References: 2 client references for similar prototype development projects

8. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY & CONFIDENTIALITY
All information shared by PARK Innovations is under NDA.
All inventions, designs, and code developed under this project shall be the exclusive property of PARK Innovations.
Your firm may retain copies for internal portfolio purposes only with written permission (anonymized until product launch).

