	('9ef7db4b-fc4c-4cd3-8813-c20a13af7513', 'Salil Arora', 'salilsarora@yahoo.co.in', '9324622693', 'Srahi', 'NA', 'Srahi is a hardware-led AI companion ecosystem specifically designed for the "Urban Silver" market. We provide a proactive, touch-first assistant that manages the daily routines and emotional connectivity of independent elders while offering quantified peace of mind to their families. Our business operates on a "hardware-light, software-margin" model, where an ergonomic physical device serves as the primary gateway for a high-trust platform of integrated services.', '0 -10 Crores INR', 'The product is an AI-enabled wearable pendant, internally referred to as the "Pebble," designed to act as a proactive companion for the Indian elderly market. Unlike reactive medical alert systems, Srahi is an "always-on" luxury butler that facilitates daily routines, emotional support, and vernacular communication.
Product Definition
• Form Factor: A sleek, ergonomic wearable (Pebble aesthetic) designed for high tactile comfort.
• Core Hardware: Based on the ESP32-S3 chipset, utilizing a BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy) bridge to offload 90% of heavy processing to a tethered smartphone.
• Primary User Interface: Voice-first and touch-responsive, optimized for "Hinglish" and regional Indian dialects (Marathi, Tamil, Kannada).
Scope of Work (SOW)
The scope is divided into three critical tracks to ensure the product is production-ready within the target price point:
1. Industrial Design & Ergonomics
• Conceptualization: Developing the physical "Pebble" form factor that emphasizes dignity over medical surveillance.
• Prototyping: Creation of functional prototypes to test weight, tactile response, and wearable attachment points (neck/pocket).
2. Design for Manufacturing (DFM)
• BOM Optimization: Finalizing the Bill of Materials to lock in a ₹1,999 target cost at scale.
• Tooling & Molds: Engineering high-precision mold development for the outer casing and internal component housing.
• Regulatory Compliance: Ensuring the design meets BIS and WPC certification standards for Indian electronics.
3. Systems Integration
• Firmware Development: Optimizing the ESP32-S3 for battery efficiency and stable BLE connectivity.
• AI Pipeline: Integration of the on-device wake-word engine with our proprietary cloud-based Personalized RAG (Memory) layer.

', '{"Industrial Design Services, Prototyping & Model Making Services, Manufacturing Readiness Services"}', '15 - 25 Lakhs (Upto 25000 USD)', '3 -4 months', 'The most important features of the Srahi "Pebble" are centered on moving away from a "medical tracking" feel toward a high-utility, respectful AI Butler experience. The primary requirements include:
1. Core Interaction & AI Intelligence
• Vernacular Voice First: The device must natively handle "Hinglish" and code-switching between English and regional dialects like Marathi, Tamil, and Kannada.
• Proprietary RAG Memory Layer: A secure, personal memory vault that allows the AI to remember past conversations, routines, and preferences, making the interaction deeply personalized over time.
• Proactive Companionship: Beyond reactive commands, the AI must initiate respectful prompts for "yoga time," medication reminders, or hydration.
2. Hardware & Industrial Design
• "Pebble" Aesthetic: A focus on high-quality industrial design that prioritizes ergonomics and dignity, ensuring the senior feels they are wearing a premium accessory rather than a surveillance tag. Primary Interface: Voice-first with a tactile,
yes/no switch—simple, familiar, and easy to use
• Optimized Connectivity: A stable BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy) bridge to a tethered smartphone, offloading 90% of heavy processing to maintain battery life and device lightness.
• Long Battery Life: The hardware must be optimized so that the wake-word engine and connectivity do not deplete the battery in a few hours.
3. Safety & Reliability
• Non-Alarming Health Alerts: A clinical-grade SOS and health-alert logic that is medically sound but communicated in a respectful, non-alarming tone.
• Trust & Compliance: Data residency compliance and necessary certifications (BIS/WPC) to ensure the platform is secure and reliable for the Indian market.

', true, 'While we are looking for the design vendor to lead the overall industrial and mechanical integration, the core of the Srahi hardware architecture is predefined based on our strategic roadmap to ensure we maintain a ₹1,999 BOM target.
We will specify or provide the following core components and architectural constraints:
• Chipset Platform: The device could be built on the ESP32-S3 base.
• Connectivity Architecture: The hardware must function as a smartphone peripheral, utilizing a BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy) bridge to offload 90% of processing tasks to the mobile application.
• AI Infrastructure: We provide the proprietary RAG-based memory systems and fine-tuned vernacular voice models for Marathi, Tamil, and Kannada that reside in our secure cloud/app layer.
• Strategic Oversight: We will provide a dedicated Manufacturing/Hardware Lead as a consultant to manage factory relations and oversee the Bill of Materials (BOM).
• UX Framework: We provide the clinical and geriatric logic for the "Butler" personality and safety layers, vetted by our Geriatric UX/Clinical Consultant.
', false, true, '2000', 'To ensure a successful partnership and maintain our target timeline, we require clarity on the following execution-level details:
1. Cost Management & DFM Expertise
• BOM Governance: How does your team approach Design for Manufacturing (DFM) to ensure the hardware doesn''t exceed our ₹1,999 target cost while maintaining a premium "Pebble" feel? 
• Vendor Ecosystem: Do you have existing relationships with Tier-1 EMS partners (e.g., in Noida or Chennai) to streamline the transition from prototyping to the first 2,000-unit production run? 
2. Technical & Regulatory Integration
• Connectivity Optimization: What is your experience in optimizing ESP32-S3 and BLE stability to ensure the "Phone-Tether" connection remains reliable without excessive battery drain? 
• Certification Support: Will your scope include the technical documentation and design iterations required for BIS and WPC certifications? 
3. Geriatric UX & Reliability
• Testing for Seniors: What is your methodology for testing tactile ergonomics and voice interface responsiveness specifically for the elderly demographic? 
• Durability & Safety: Since this is a wearable for seniors, what are your standards for drop-testing, sweat resistance, and hypoallergenic material selection for the casing? 
4. Timeline & Milestones
• Phased Delivery: Can you provide a breakdown of your internal milestones to align with our 15–18 month runway, specifically targeting the delivery of production-ready moulds within the first two quarters? 

