As of now, I have withheld the company at this stage but to give a background we are battery storage systems manufacturer for solar power applications. ', 4, 'Google', '2026-07-15', '11:00 AM', NULL, '2026-07-14 12:16:23.568+00', '[{"id":"reminder-1785225384775-oesypm","to":"sobhan06@gmail.com","subject":"Techno - Commercial offer update follow up","body":"Hi Sobhan Babu Kumar,\n\n                                                    Greetings to you!\n\n                                                    Just checking in to see if you had a chance to review our Techno Commercial offer in detail.\n\n                                                    We can arrange a quick 15 minutes meeting to explain in detail if required.\n\n                                                    If you have any questions, please reply to this email. We are happy to help.\n\n                                                    Awaiting your positive response!\n\n                                                    Regards,\n                                                    Team Iuova.","sentAt":"2026-07-28T07:56:24.775Z","status":"sent","direction":"outbound","source":"rfq-reminder-manual","gmailMessageId":"<90e8d780-790a-fe81-fe83-1dc3981255ea@iuova.in>","messageIdHeader":"<90e8d780-790a-fe81-fe83-1dc3981255ea@iuova.in>"}]', 'https://meet.google.com/spc-djzz-njo', NULL, '<2e0bbca6-a1a8-4619-af68-75cf5431fd87@iuova.in>', '<90e8d780-790a-fe81-fe83-1dc3981255ea@iuova.in>', true, true, '2026-07-17 10:04:36.916+00', 'Product Design and Delivery', true, NULL, NULL),
	('5570a233-04cb-4eb0-b65b-ce72786e4286', 'anesh vrindavan', 'avrindav@amazon.com', '6364060608', 'Amazon', 'https://www.amazon.com/', 'E-commerce ', '1000 Crores INR and above', 'Currently, employees who lose their badge or new joiners who need a permanent badge must wait 10-15 minutes at the security desk for manual verification and badge issuance. This creates queues, dependency on on-site security staff, and impacts productivity. The Badge Kiosk eliminates this bottleneck by providing a fully self-service experience that completes the entire process — from identity verification to hard badge printing — in under 3 minutes. The system uses multi-factor authentication (Amazon alias, phone verification, and AI-powered photo comparison) without storing biometric data, maintaining compliance with Amazon''s privacy and security policies. Expected outcome is a 60-70% reduction in security desk workload for badge-related requests.', '{"Product Design Services (Industrial Design)"}', '20 Lakhs and Above (Above 25000 USD)', '1 - 2 months', 'The kiosk is an enclosed oval/capsule-shaped pod, approximately 1300mm wide × 1200mm deep × 2300mm tall, constructed from lightweight aluminium that is rust-resistant and durable. The exterior is white powder-coated with Amazon branding (navy and orange logo). The pod features a transparent glass front panel with an electronically controlled door that unlocks via RFID badge swipe. The design must be modular — easy to dismantle, fold, pack, and transport without special tools, with assembly achievable in under 30 minutes. Interior walls are matte white (non-reflective for photography) with basic acoustic padding for privacy. The pod includes a height-adjustable stool (450-700mm range), professional LED ring lighting at 5500K daylight color temperature for even illumination, and internal cable management that is fully concealed from the user. Power requirement is a single standard 230V/16A inlet to supply all internal systems. Target total weight is under 150 kg fully assembled.', true, 'The kiosk integrates the following hardware systems: An HID iCLASS-compatible RFID/NFC card reader at the entrance for access control, with red/green LED indicator and electromagnetic door lock. Inside, a 21-27 inch IPS display (1080p minimum) serves as the main screen for operator video calls, welcome messages, and queue status. A separate 10-12 inch touchscreen tablet mounted at eye level allows the employee to type their alias, review their photo, and confirm printing. A professional auto-focus camera (5MP minimum) with LED ring light captures the badge photo, with face detection and auto-framing software ensuring consistent results. The badge printing system uses a Roland VersaUV LEF-200 UV flatbed inkjet printer with UV-LED curing technology, producing hard PVC plastic badges at up to 1440 × 1440 dpi resolution using CMYK + White + Clear + Primer inks. The printer connects via USB 2.0 or Ethernet and uses Roland VersaWorks RIP software. Print time is approximately 60-90 seconds per badge. Dispensers are provided for the printed badge, yoyo retractable badge reels, clear plastic badge holders, and lanyards — each with minimum 50-unit capacity per refill cycle. An embedded mini-PC inside the pod runs the web-based kiosk software and handles all API communications over Ethernet (primary) or Wi-Fi (backup).', true, false, NULL, 'nil 
