	('2f813b89-ad68-44a3-a586-3ec67ae9f2dd', 'Anuj Chandalia', 'anuj.chandalia99@gmail.com', '07283964334', 'New startup ', 'Yet to Decided', 'health technology company developing next-generation AI-powered wearable devices for continuous monitoring of cardiovascular, neurological, and wellness biomarkers. Our flagship product, VivaraPatch, is an ultra-thin, behind-the-ear wearable designed to provide clinical-grade health insights while remaining comfortable for everyday use. Unlike traditional smartwatches, VivaraPatch is positioned over the mastoid region to capture high-quality physiological signals using a multi-sensor platform that combines ECG, ear-EEG, PPG, temperature, motion (IMU), and other biosensors.', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'The proposed product is an ultra-thin, behind-the-ear wearable health intelligence device designed to continuously monitor cardiovascular, neurological, and physiological signals using a multi-sensor platform. Positioned over the mastoid region, the device integrates dry ECG, ear-EEG, PPG, temperature, IMU, and optional GSR sensors with low-power edge AI to provide continuous health insights while remaining comfortable for up to 15 days of wear. The initial prototype will focus on core capabilities including heart rate and heart rate variability, irregular heart rhythm awareness, sleep staging, sleep apnoea screening, fatigue and drowsiness detection, stress monitoring, body temperature trends, fall detection, circadian rhythm tracking, and balance monitoring.

The scope of work includes human-factor studies, ergonomic design, industrial design, mechanical enclosure development, flexible PCB architecture, sensor placement optimization, electronics integration, firmware development, BLE connectivity, companion mobile application integration, and cloud-based data visualization. The project will also include CAD modelling, prototype fabrication, rapid iteration through 3D printing and flexible electronics, functional testing, signal validation, battery optimization, adhesive and skin-contact evaluation, and preparation for engineering validation testing (EVT). The final deliverable will be a fully functional engineering prototype with complete mechanical, electrical, and software documentation, providing a foundation for regulatory testing, clinical validation, and future design-for-manufacturing (DFM) activities.', '{"Product Design Services (Industrial Design)"}', '5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)', '1 - 2 months', 'The product should be an ultra-thin, lightweight, medical-grade wearable patch designed to sit discreetly behind the ear over the mastoid bone, enabling continuous monitoring without affecting daily activities or sleep. It should provide reliable multi-sensor health monitoring by integrating ECG, ear-EEG, PPG, skin temperature, IMU (6-axis motion sensor), and GSR electrodes on a flexible PCB with optimized sensor placement for high-quality signal acquisition. The device should support up to 15 days of continuous operation on a single battery, offer IP68 water resistance, medical-grade skin-safe adhesive, Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE 5.3) connectivity, and secure on-device AI processing with encrypted cloud synchronization. Key health capabilities should include heart rate, heart rate variability, atrial fibrillation and irregular rhythm detection, sleep staging, sleep apnoea screening, fatigue and drowsiness monitoring, stress analysis, body temperature trends, fever detection, fall detection, fertility and circadian rhythm tracking, and balance/vestibular assessment. The enclosure should be ergonomic, ultra-low profile (approximately 60 × 40 × 2.5 mm), comfortable for long-term wear, and designed to fit beneath the hairline with minimal visibility. The product should also support firmware updates, smartphone integration, real-time alerts, clinician data sharing, and a scalable architecture for future regulatory approval and AI-based predictive health analytics.', false, NULL, false, false, NULL, 'Yet to decide', 5, 'Google', '2026-07-28', '11:00 AM', '["https://oscdtdlwdrwvjvteqcix.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/video%20and%20image/1784879776786-tn84rg.png"]', '2026-07-24 07:56:17.996+00', '[{"id":"reply-reminder-1785209409628","to":"anuj.chandalia99@gmail.com","cc":["crm@iuova.in","info@iuova.in","support@iuova.in"],"subject":"Reminder: Your IUOVA meeting is today","body":"Hi Anuj Chandalia,\n\nThis is a reminder that your meeting is today.\n\nDate: Tuesday, July 28, 2026\nTime: 11:00 AM (Asia/Kolkata)\nMeeting link: https://meet.google.com/hxn-eivx-ojc\n\nIf you need to reschedule, just reply to this email.\n\nRegards,\nIUOVA Team","sentAt":"2026-07-28T03:30:09.628Z","status":"sent","templateId":"meeting-reminder-today","messageIdHeader":"<b1737c81-c3c5-3901-b50e-2d8b3509f89d@iuova.in>","references_id":"<4fbc455e-196e-be17-2d07-a06cc6019a50@iuova.in> <21cd85c8-0ec8-c518-08aa-62fdac0a4278@iuova.in>","gmailThreadId":null,"direction":"outbound","source":"smtp"},{"id":"reply-1785152138229","to":"anuj.chandalia99@gmail.com","cc":["info@iuova.in","crm@iuova.in, waseet@iuova.in, anirudha@iuova.in"],"subject":"Missed Meeting - Reschedule Request","body":"Dear Anuj Chandalia,\n\nWe hope you''re doing well.\n\nIt seems we couldn''t connect for our scheduled online meeting today. We understand that unexpected commitments can arise.\n\nPlease let us know a convenient date and time for you, and we''ll be happy to reschedule the meeting. We look forward to connecting with you.\n\