.in>', false, false, NULL, 'Yet to Decided', false, NULL, NULL),
	('93008501-2f59-40dd-bdb6-c5c9f9248929', 'Priyanka Agarwal', 'priyanka.nivara@gmail.com', '07665918025', 'Nivara Life Pvt. Ltd.', 'no website ', 'Nivara Life is not incorporated yet but it aims to be a consumer appliance company meant for modern, accessible and low-water/energy usage portable needs of new modern and minimalistic living ', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'A compact countertop dishwasher, sized for 2 people or a small household’s dishes, that needs no plumbing connection and no mains electrical wiring. It runs on 12V DC, delivered through a standard USB-C Power Delivery charger or a solar power bank. It has no heating element — the user pours in already-hot water. The machine runs a full automatic wash-and-rinse cycle from a single pour of water, using a passive mechanical mechanism to split that one pour into a wash volume and a separate, clean rinse volume, with no second fill, no second pump, and no electronically controlled valve sequencing to achieve the split.', '{"Prototyping Services","Product Analysis Services","Manufacturing Services"}', '5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)', '1 - 2 months', 'I can share all details post NDA signing and discussion', false, NULL, false, false, NULL, 'Product Category: Home appliances
Organization Type: Individual entrepreneur or inventor

I would like to sign an NDA before revealing more details and exact engineering drawings/features. Provisional patent filing is pending ', 4, 'Google', '2026-09-24', '05:00 PM', NULL, '2026-09-21 10:35:41.011+00', '[{"id":"reply-reminder-1790220605715","to":"priyanka.nivara@gmail.com","cc":["crm@iuova.in","info@iuova.in","support@iuova.in"],"subject":"Reminder: Your IUOVA meeting is today","body":"Hi Priyanka Agarwal,\n\nThis is a reminder that your meeting is today.\n\nDate: Thursday, September 24, 2026\nTime: 05:00 PM (Asia/Kolkata)\nMeeting link: https://meet.google.com/uzv-krxt-jmg\n\nIf you need to reschedule, just reply to this email.\n\nRegards,\nIUOVA Team","sentAt":"2026-09-24T03:30:05.715Z","status":"sent","templateId":"meeting-reminder-today","messageIdHeader":"<627fff3a-a1a3-4243-7f4c-2d5a456c6f35@iuova.in>","references_id":"<fe157823-41d0-4f75-5450-314dda86d9f5@iuova.in> <b3bb3798-df7f-ce45-d68f-277e5d6cf518@iuova.in>","gmailThreadId":null,"direction":"outbound","source":"smtp"}]', 'https://meet.google.com/uzv-krxt-jmg', 'k3r819i9mgf27v9srr4hm1pcug', '<b3bb3798-df7f-ce45-d68f-277e5d6cf518@iuova.in>', '<fe157823-41d0-4f75-5450-314dda86d9f5@iuova.in>', false, false, NULL, 'Nivara BD-1', false, 'Home appliances', 'Individual entrepreneur or inventor'),
	('39360610-13aa-46dd-a95b-edac22dfefa9', 'Shamil SK', 'shamilsk1911@gmail.com', '+919048050233, +97471859508', 'Startup', 'NIL', 'Dear Team,

I am exploring the development of a compact, purpose-built handheld e-paper device and am looking for a product-development partner who can support the project from concept and engineering through prototype and production readiness.

Concept
The device should be small, pocketable, reasonably thin, simple, power-efficient and affordable, using a monochrome/ e-paper display.

My preferred starting point is around 3.7 inches, but this is flexible. I understand that display availability, resolution, readability, MOQ, battery, cost and engineering requirements may require changes to the screen size or overall dimensions.

The device would use a lightweight, minimal software environment, with an Android/iOS companion app handling more complex functions such as configuration, book/content transfer, synchronization and secure firmware/software updates.

Key priorities are:
* Excellent multilingual text rendering and multiple font support
* Good e-paper readability
* Long battery life and low standby consumption
* Fast, stable operation
* Secure and upgradeable firmware/software architecture
* Reasonable hardware headroom for future updates
* Compact, durable design
* *Low eventual manufacturing cost*

Affordability is fundamental. The architecture should therefore be designed with mass-production economics in mind from the beginning.

Development Support Required
I am approaching this from the product/business side rather than as a hardware engineer,
1. System architecture
2. Component selection and BOM
3. Schematic and PCB development
4. E-paper integration
5. Firmware and lightweight OS/software
6. Power optimization
7. Android/iOS companion application
8. Mechanical/industrial design
9. Prototype manufacturing and assembly
10. Testing and optimization
11. Production engineering/DFM
12. Manufacturing/scaling support

Initial Assessment Required
Before developing detailed specifications, I would like to understand:
1. Is the overall concept technically feasible, even with necessary changes?
2. What architecture would you recommend?
3. What e-paper panels would be suitable considering size, resolution, availability, MOQ and cost?
4. What development stages would you recommend?
5. What should the prototype approach be?
6. What is the expected development timeline?
7. What approximate development/prototype budget should I expect?
8. Can this realistically be manufactured and sold as a *budget-friendly consumer product* at scale?
9. What major technical, cost or manufacturing risks/compromises do you foresee?


My immediate objective is to understand:
Can this be built? What changes are needed? What would it approximately cost to develop? And can it eventually be manufactured and sold at an affordable price?

If the initial assessment is positive, I can proceed with a detailed product requirements document.

Best regards,
Shamil SK', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'Dear Team,

