 ---------- Forwarded message ---------\r\n>> From: Nikhil Sankpal <n.sankpal@zitrushealthcare.com>\r\n>> Date: Fri, 29 May 2026, 19:42\r\n>> Subject: Request for Technical Support & Quotation – 46L Class B Steam\r\n>> Sterilizer Development\r\n>> To: <support@iuova.in>\r\n>> Cc: Shivram <shivram@zitrushealthcare.com>, info@zitrushealthcare.com <\r\n>> info@zitrushealthcare.com>\r\n>>\r\n>>\r\n>>\r\n>> Dear Sir,\r\n>> We are currently working on the development of a 46 Liter Class B Steam\r\n>> Sterilizer, which is essentially an upscaled version of our existing 23\r\n>> Liter model.\r\n>> For this project, we are looking for technical support and engineering\r\n>> consultation in both theoretical and practical aspects related to the\r\n>> system design, component selection, and performance optimization.\r\n>> We would like to understand the level of technical support your team can\r\n>> provide in the following areas:\r\n>>\r\n>>    - Steam chamber design and calculations\r\n>>    - Vacuum pump selection and performance calculations\r\n>>    - Steam generator design and heater sizing\r\n>>    - Radiator / condenser selection\r\n>>    - Door locking and safety mechanism design\r\n>>    - Heater specifications and optimization\r\n>>    - Selection and integration of control sensors such as:\r\n>>    - RTD sensors\r\n>>       - Thermostats\r\n>>       - Pressure sensors\r\n>>       - Safety valves and related control components\r\n>>       - Vacuum and pressure cycle performance optimization\r\n>>    - System efficiency and process validation considerations\r\n>>\r\n>> We would appreciate support in terms of:\r\n>>\r\n>>    - Design calculations\r\n>>    - Technical recommendations\r\n>>    - Component sizing and selection\r\n>>    - Practical implementation guidance\r\n>>    - Troubleshooting and performance improvement suggestions\r\n>>\r\n>> Kindly let us know:\r\n>>\r\n>>    1. The scope and level of technical support your organization can\r\n>>    provide\r\n>>    2. Whether you offer consultation on a project basis or milestone\r\n>>    basis\r\n>>    3. Expected timelines for support\r\n>>    4. Commercial terms and quotation for your services\r\n>>\r\n>> Please feel free to share any additional details regarding your technical\r\n>> capabilities, previous experience in sterilizer/autoclave systems, and\r\n>> standard support process.\r\n>> Looking forward to your response.\r\n>> Best Regards,\r\n>> Nikhil Sankpal\r\n>>\r\n>>\r\n>>\r\n>>\r\n>\r\n> --\r\n>\r\n>\r\n> *Rupali SirsathBusiness Development Executive*\r\n> M: +91 - *81044 87664*\r\n> IUOVA PRODUCT DESIGN COMPANY\r\n> 504, Filix Tower, Mulund Goregaon Link Rd, Mulund West- 400080, Mumbai,\r\n> Maharashtra\r\n> iuovadesign.com\r\n>\r\n\r\n\r\n-- \r\n*\"Note: We recommend Prototyping and Validation Analysis before\r\nManufacturing/Tooling (where applicable).\"*\r\n\r\nThanks & Regards\r\n\r\n\r\n*Waseet Saad*\r\n\r\n*Engineering Manager **(M: +91-9767342679)*\r\n\r\n*Disclaimer - Breach of confidentiality*\r\n\r\nThis email and its attachments are confidential and intended solely for the\r\nrecipient. If you have received it in error, please notify the sender\r\nimmediately and delete it. Unauthorized use, disclosure, or distribution is\r\nprohibited.","sentAt":"2026-06-05T13:02:04.000Z","status":"sent","templateId":"techno-commercial","messageIdHeader":"<CALNTVuKeDdwABa-Q0Rk8vwMv3Q7Pkx5naoXcJCoTcxP--yWJDw@mail.gmail.com>","gmailThreadId":"19e7414a6224e71f","references":null,"direction":"outbound","source":"gmail-sent"},{"id":"reply-reminder-1780371006174","to":"n.sankpal@zitrushealthcare.com","cc":["developer@iuova.in","info@iuova.in","support@iuova.in"],"subject":"Reminder: IUOVA Meeting on Wednesday, June 3, 2026 at 11:00 AM (Asia/Kolkata) - tomorrow","body":"Hi Nikhil,\n\nThis is a reminder that your meeting is tomorrow.\n\nDate: Wednesday, June 3, 2026\nTime: 11:00 AM (Asia/Kolkata)\nMeeting link: https://meet.google.com/cni-hihx-fie\n\nIf you need to reschedule, just reply to this email.\n\nRegards,\nIUOVA Team","sentAt":"2026-06-02T03:30:06.175Z","status":"sent","templateId":"meeting-reminder-tomorrow","messageIdHeader":"<bc48fb27-47d4-36cc-e6e3-49383b7e83f6@iuova.in>","gmailThreadId":null,"references":null,"direction":"outbound","source":"smtp"}]', 'https://meet.google.com/cni-hihx-fie', NULL, '<ce1b543e-3224-2a0f-eb89-9c586b397e10@iuova.in>', '<d3976104-19a9-38a8-15a6-0bc7904ab3d4@iuova.in>', true, true, '2026-06-06 03:30:10.915+00', 'Table Top class B steam sterilizer', true, NULL, NULL),
	('5570a233-04cb-4eb0-b65b-ce72786e4286', 'anesh vrindavan', 'avrindav@amazon.com', '6364060608', 'Amazon', 'https://www.amazon.com/', 'E-commerce ', '1000 Crores INR and above', 'Currently, employees who lose their badge or new joiners who need a permanent badge must wait 10-15 minutes at the security desk for manual verification and badge issuance. This creates queues, dependency on on-site security staff, and impacts productivity. The Badge Kiosk eliminates this bottleneck by providing a fully self-service experience that completes the entire process — from identity verification to hard badge printing — in under 3 minutes. The system uses multi-factor authentication (Amazon alias, phone verification, and AI-powered photo comparison) without storing biometric data, maintaining compliance with Amazon''s privacy and security policies. Expected outcome is a 60-70% reduction in security desk workload for badge-related requests.', '{"Product Design Services (Industrial Design)"}', '20 Lakhs and Above (Above 25000 USD)', '1 - 2 months', 'The kiosk is an enclosed oval/capsule-shaped pod, approximately 1300mm wide × 1200mm deep × 2300mm tall, constructed from lightweight aluminium that is rust-resistant and durable. The exterior is white powder-coated with Amazon branding (navy and orange logo). The pod features a transparent glass front panel with an electronically controlled door that unlocks via RFID badge swipe. The design must be modular — easy to dismantle, fold, pack, and transport without special tools, with assembly achievable in under 30 minutes. Interior walls are matte white (non-reflective for photography) with basic acoustic padding for privacy. The pod includes a height-adjustable stool (450-700mm range), professional LED ring lighting at 5500K daylight color temperature for even illumination, and internal cable management that is fully concealed from the user. Power requirement is a single standard 230V/16A inlet to supply all internal systems. Target total weight is under 150 kg fully assembled.', true, 'The kiosk integrates the following hardware systems: An HID iCLASS-compatible RFID/NFC card reader at the entrance for access control, with red/green LED indicator and electromagnetic door lock. Inside, a 21-27 inch IPS display (1080p minimum) serves as the main screen for operator video calls, welcome messages, and queue status. A separate 10-12 inch touchscreen tablet mounted at eye level allows the employee to type their alias, review their photo, and confirm printing. A professional auto-focus camera (5MP minimum) with LED ring light captures the badge photo, with face detection and auto-framing software ensuring consistent results. The badge printing system uses a Roland VersaUV LEF-200 UV flatbed inkjet printer with UV-LED curing technology, producing hard PVC plastic badges at up to 1440 × 1440 dpi resolution using CMYK + White + Clear + Primer inks. The printer connects via USB 2.0 or Ethernet and uses Roland VersaWorks RIP software. Print time is approximately 60-90 seconds per badge. Dispensers are provided for the printed badge, yoyo retractable badge reels, clear plastic badge holders, and lanyards — each with minimum 50-unit capacity per refill cycle. An embedded mini-PC inside the pod runs the web-based kiosk software and handles all API communications over Ethernet (primary) or Wi-Fi (backup).', true, false, NULL, 'nil 
', 5, 'Google', '2026-07-27', '03:00 PM', '["https://oscdtdlwdrwvjvteqcix.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/video%20and%20image/1784799087707-toejdu7.png"]', '2026-07-23 09:31:28.799+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, false, false, NULL, 'Next-Generation Automated Badge Issuance Kiosk', false, NULL, NULL),
	('2f813b89-ad68-44a3-a586-3ec67ae9f2dd', 'Anuj Chandalia', 'anuj.chandalia99@gmail.com', '07283964334', 'New startup ', 'Yet to Decided', 'health technology company developing next-generation AI-powered wearable devices for continuous monitoring of cardiovascular, neurological, and wellness biomarkers. Our flagship product, VivaraPatch, is an ultra-thin, behind-the-ear wearable designed to provide clinical-grade health insights while remaining comfortable for everyday use. Unlike traditional smartwatches, VivaraPatch is positioned over the mastoid region to capture high-quality physiological signals using a multi-sensor platform that combines ECG, ear-EEG, PPG, temperature, motion (IMU), and other biosensors.', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'The proposed product is an ultra-thin, behind-the-ear wearable health intelligence device designed to continuously monitor cardiovascular, neurological, and physiological signals using a multi-sensor platform. Positioned over the mastoid region, the device integrates dry ECG, ear-EEG, PPG, temperature, IMU, and optional GSR sensors with low-power edge AI to provide continuous health insights while remaining comfortable for up to 15 days of wear. The initial prototype will focus on core capabilities including heart rate and heart rate variability, irregular heart rhythm awareness, sleep staging, sleep apnoea screening, fatigue and drowsiness detection, stress monitoring, body temperature trends, fall detection, circadian rhythm tracking, and balance monitoring.

The scope of work includes human-factor studies, ergonomic design, industrial design, mechanical enclosure development, flexible PCB architecture, sensor placement optimization, electronics integration, firmware development, BLE connectivity, companion mobile application integration, and cloud-based data visualization. The project will also include CAD modelling, prototype fabrication, rapid iteration through 3D printing and flexible electronics, functional testing, signal validation, battery optimization, adhesive and skin-contact evaluation, and preparation for engineering validation testing (EVT). The final deliverable will be a fully functional engineering prototype with complete mechanical, electrical, and software documentation, providing a foundation for regulatory testing, clinical validation, and future design-for-manufacturing (DFM) activities.', '{"Product Design Services (Industrial Design)"}', '5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)', '1 - 2 months', 'The product should be an ultra-thin, lightweight, medical-grade wearable patch designed to sit discreetly behind the ear over the mastoid bone, enabling continuous monitoring without affecting daily activities or sleep. It should provide reliable multi-sensor health monitoring by integrating ECG, ear-EEG, PPG, skin temperature, IMU (6-axis motion sensor), and GSR electrodes on a flexible PCB with optimized sensor placement for high-quality signal acquisition. The device should support up to 15 days of continuous operation on a single battery, offer IP68 water resistance, medical-grade skin-safe adhesive, Bluetooth Low Energy (BLE 5.3) connectivity, and secure on-device AI processing with encrypted cloud synchronization. Key health capabilities should include heart rate, heart rate variability, atrial fibrillation and irregular rhythm detection, sleep staging, sleep apnoea screening, fatigue and drowsiness monitoring, stress analysis, body temperature trends, fever detection, fall detection, fertility and circadian rhythm tracking, and balance/vestibular assessment. The enclosure should be ergonomic, ultra-low profile (approximately 60 × 40 × 2.5 mm), comfortable for long-term wear, and designed to fit beneath the hairline with minimal visibility. The product should also support firmware updates, smartphone integration, real-time alerts, clinician data sharing, and a scalable architecture for future regulatory approval and AI-based predictive health analytics.', false, NULL, false, false, NULL, 'Yet to decide', 5, 'Google', '2026-07-27', '05:00 PM', '["https://oscdtdlwdrwvjvteqcix.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/video%20and%20image/1784879776786-tn84rg.png"]', '2026-07-24 07:56:17.996+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, false, false, NULL, 'Yet to Decided', false, NULL, NULL),
	('4fb9b1e1-726c-4018-a17e-8968e5c710ef', 'Victor Villazon', 'victor.villazon@villazoncode.com', '015754390209', 'Villazon Code', 'Under development / Pre-launch stage ([www.villazoncode.com]', 'Villazon Code is an emerging, pre-launch Berlin-based menswear and accessories brand with a strong focus on hardware implementation, kinetic structures, and custom metalwork in its designs.', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'Development of a high-end, kinetic articulated bodypiece shaped as a snake, designed to drape ergonomically across the torso and function as a standalone sculpture when off the body. Scope of work includes: 3D CAD engineering from concept renders, designing hidden multi-link joints/mechanisms, SLA prototyping for physical fit tests, and batch manufacturing setup (investment casting preparation, hand assembly, and electroplating oversight).', '{"Product Design Services (Industrial Design)","Product Engineering Services","Prototyping Services","Manufacturing Services"}', 'Budget to be finalized upon review of the technical scope and RFQ proposal post-NDA execution. Target is low-volume / batch manufacturing development.', '2 - 3 months', '1. Dual-Purpose Architecture: Ergonomic, fluid draping across the human torso when worn, while maintaining self-supporting structural balance as a standalone sculpture when on display.

2. Modular Kinetic Mechanics: Multi-link articulated structure with concealed micro-hinges and smooth pivot movement.

3. Internal Mechanism Integration: Dedicated internal housing within the links for functional/sound mechanisms.

4. Production Readiness: Precision micro-casting tolerances (brass/bronze), gem setting alignment, and concealed brand hallmarking.', false, NULL, false, true, '1 Golden Sample (Master Prototype for marketing and pre-order launch), followed by low-volume batches (10–20 units per batch).', 'NDA & Design Brief: We look forward to receiving the countersigned NDA so we can share our concept PDF, reference renders, and design preferences prior to our scheduled call.', 5, 'Google', '2026-07-29', '03:00 PM', NULL, '2026-07-28 10:46:56.034+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, false, false, NULL, 'Sculptural Articulated Bodypiece (Kinetic Hardware)', false, NULL, NULL),
