	('a6170ef5-e802-4573-a974-34b8f61ae715', 'Kottapalli Vamsi', 'vamsikottapallimfgengg@gmail.com', '6300671877', 'TapCook', 'None', 'TapCook is a FoodTech startup developing smart, automated kitchen appliances that make everyday cooking more convenient and accessible. Our flagship product is a remotely operated smart rice-cooking appliance that automates rice dispensing, washing, water measurement, and cooking, allowing users to initiate and monitor the cooking process through a mobile application. We aim to combine IoT, automation, and intelligent kitchen technology to simplify cooking for busy households and working professionals.
', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'Product Description

TapCook is a smart, automated rice-cooking appliance designed to automate the complete rice-cooking process with minimal user intervention. The system will store rice and water, automatically dispense the required quantity, wash the rice, transfer it to the cooking chamber, and cook it according to the selected quantity/program. The appliance will be designed with IoT connectivity to enable remote operation and monitoring through a mobile application.

The MVP will focus on developing a functional, safe, compact and aesthetically designed working prototype demonstrating the complete automated cooking cycle.

Scope of Work

The development scope shall include:

1. Industrial & Mechanical Design

   * Finalize overall product architecture and dimensions.
   * Design the external enclosure with a premium consumer-appliance appearance.
   * Design rice hopper, water tank, washing chamber and cooking chamber integration.
   * Develop mechanisms for rice dispensing, water dispensing, washing, transfer and drainage.
   * Provide 3D CAD models, detailed mechanical drawings and assembly drawings.

2. Electronics & Control System

   * Design the electronic control architecture.
   * Integrate microcontroller/IoT connectivity, sensors, motors, solenoid valves and necessary drivers.
   * Develop PCB/electronics integration suitable for the MVP.
   * Implement monitoring of water/rice flow and key operating conditions.
   * Include appropriate electrical and operational safety provisions.

3. Embedded Software / Firmware

   * Develop firmware for automatic sequencing of the cooking process.
   * Control rice dispensing, water filling, washing, transfer, drainage and cooking operations.
   * Implement sensor feedback, error detection and basic safety logic.

4. IoT & Mobile Application – MVP

   * Enable remote start/stop and basic monitoring of the appliance.
   * Develop basic communication between the appliance and mobile application/cloud platform.
   * Provide essential user controls and cooking-status information.

5. Prototype Development

   * Manufacture/assemble the complete functional prototype.
   * Integrate mechanical, electrical, electronic and software components.
   * Conduct functional testing and debugging.
   * Demonstrate complete automated rice-cooking cycle.

6. Testing & Validation

   * Test rice and water dispensing accuracy.
   * Validate washing, transfer, drainage and cooking operations.
   * Test electrical, mechanical and operational safety.
   * Identify and rectify major prototype-level issues.

7. Final Deliverables

   * Fully assembled functional TapCook MVP prototype.
   * 3D CAD and manufacturing drawings.
   * BOM (Bill of Materials).
   * Electrical/electronic schematics.
   * PCB design files, where applicable.
   * Embedded firmware.
   * Basic IoT/mobile application MVP.
   * Prototype testing and validation report.
   * Assembly and operating documentation.

The primary objective is to develop a functional end-to-end TapCook MVP that demonstrates automated rice dispensing, washing, water dispensing, transfer and cooking, with basic IoT-based remote operation.', '{"Product Engineering Services","Product Design Services (Industrial Design)","Prototyping Services","Manufacturing Services"}', '5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)', '2 - 3 months', 'Essential Features – TapCook MVP

1. Automatic Rice Dispensing
 – Controlled dispensing of the required quantity of rice from the rice hopper.

2. Automatic Water Dispensing
– Accurate dispensing of the required quantity of water.

3. Automatic Rice Washing
– Automated washing/rinsing of rice before cooking.

4. Automatic Rice Transfer
– Automatic transfer of washed rice and water to the cooking chamber.

5. Automatic Cooking
 – Integrated cooking chamber with automatic temperature and cooking-time control.

6. Full Water Wash / Self-Cleaning Cycle
 – A dedicated app option to flush and clean the internal pipes, water lines, valves and washing chamber, with used water drained after cleaning.

7. IoT Connectivity
– Wireless connectivity between the appliance and mobile application.

8. Mobile App Control
– Remote start, stop and monitoring of the appliance.

9. Rice Level Status in App
– Real-time display of the rice level/quantity remaining in the rice hopper.

10. Water Level Status in App
– Real-time display of the water level/quantity remaining in the water tank.

11. Real-Time Process Status
– Display of the current operating stage, such as Ready → Dispensing → Washing → Transferring → Cooking → Completed.

12. Sensors & Feedback
– Rice-level, water-level, flow, position and other necessary sensors for reliable automated operation.

13. Safety Features
– Protection against overheating, overflow, leakage, dry running and other operating risks.

14. Manual Override & Emergency Stop
– Ability to safely stop the system and provide manual control during testing or emergencies.

15. Food-Grade & Hygienic Design – Suitable food-grade materials for food/water-contacting components with provisions for easy cleaning.

16. Compact Premium Product Design
– Enclosed, aesthetically appealing and practical product architecture suitable for future commercial production.
', false, NULL, false, true, 'Function Prototype for Manufacturing (1 No)', 'We are looking for an end-to-end development partner who can support **TapCook from detailed engineering and prototype development to testing and functional validation**. The MVP should be designed with **modularity, reliability, hygiene, safety and future scalability for commercial production** in mind. We would also like the development partner to provide complete technical documentation, BOM, CAD/design files, electronics/PCB files and firmware/software source files developed as part of the project. The final prototype should demonstrate the complete automated cooking and self-cleaning functionality under practical operating conditions.
