	('47c85fbd-ac3b-4ae5-b4cb-071ef7bbf86b', 'Shama Meghe', 'shamarajan9@gmail.com', '9820604757', 'The bombay balance ', 'Thebombaybalance.co', 'Bombay Balance — App Concept

Bombay Balance is a modern holistic wellbeing platform built around the idea that true wellbeing comes from balancing the whole person — body, breath, mind, emotions and deeper sense of self.

The brand currently offers meditation, breathwork, somatic movement, sound and community experiences. Its existing programming includes movement flows, sound baths and meditation courses. ', '0 - 10 Crores INR', 'We want to take the Bombay Balance method online and make it interactive, beautiful and easy to use — more like a modern fitness/wellness app than a traditional meditation app.

The core experience will combine:

* Meditation — guided practices for stillness, focus and mental clarity
* Breathwork — short practices for regulating energy and state
* Somatic Movement — movement sequences to release tension and reconnect with the body
* Sound — soundscapes, sound meditation and eventually immersive audio
* Knowledge — short, digestible lessons explaining the why behind each practice
* Daily rituals — personalised recommendations based on how the user is feeling
* Progress / self-awareness — helping users understand patterns in their mental, emotional and physical state

The USP

The key difference is that Bombay Balance isn’t just a meditation library.

It’s intended to become an interactive nervous-system and self-awareness platform where users learn:

“What do I need right now?” → “Which practice will help me shift my state?”

Eventually, the app should build a knowledge graph of the user — connecting their moods, energy, sleep, stress, practices and responses over time — and use that information to personalise their experience.

MVP

For version 1, I would keep it very simple:

Home → Check-in → Recommended Practice → Video/Audio Practice → Reflection → Progress

Start with your own content and your own voice rather than trying to build a huge content library.

The first version could have ~30–40 pieces of content across meditation, breathwork and somatic movement, with a very premium, editorial visual identity.

Think: Sweat × Headspace × nervous-system education — but distinctly Bombay Balance.', '{"Prototyping Services"}', 'Don’t have ', '0 - 1 months', 'We want to take the Bombay Balance method online and make it interactive, beautiful and easy to use — more like a modern fitness/wellness app than a traditional meditation app.

