Vatsal Gudhka", "exec_investment_summary": "Total engagement of 9-10 weeks at the Foundation package level. Investment from ₹16.7L (Foundation) to ₹21.2L (Flagship), excluding GST and prototype costs at actuals."}', '2026-07-22 10:16:17.456741+00', '2026-07-22 10:16:17.456741+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('tc_na6bdoc2w', 'Mersiv Labs LLP', 'Blob', 'Eshaan Mehta', '', '9819918315', '{NULL,NULL,NULL}', 2535000, 'Sent', '{"fx": 90, "tc": [{"items": ["The Client shall provide complete and detailed information before project commencement to ensure accurate delivery."], "title": "Project Initiation"}, {"items": ["Client must make payments as per payment schedule in agreement, delay in payments more that 30 days will incur additional delay charges of 5% of total fees and work will be halted. It will commence once payments are cleared.", "Invoicing need to complete within 7 days of milestone completion.", "Travelling will be billed as per actual for onsite client or vendor visits."], "title": "Payment Terms"}, {"items": ["We will provide fair concepts based on client inputs and feedback.", "Clients are allowed up to three revisions; additional revisions will incur extra charges as mutually agreed.", "Modifications after finalizing the design and CAD files will be treated as additional scope of work and will incur additional charges as mutually agreed."], "title": "Concept Development and Revisions"}, {"items": ["Client-induced delays exceeding 2 months will incur waiting charges of 10% of the total fees per delayed week.", "Client must make complete payment once the services are delivered by IUOVA, till that ownership of the developed Design/Product associated with the project remains with IUOVA."], "title": "Delays and Waiting Charges"}, {"items": ["Work outside the original scope of work will be charged based on the quantum of work or a mutually agreed value."], "title": "Additional Work"}, {"items": ["Mutual consent is required for project cancellation.", "Client-initiated cancellations: advance payments are non-refundable.", "IUOVA-initiated cancellations (due to client fault): client must clear payments for work done."], "title": "Project Cancellation"}, {"items": ["Any information that is publicly available will not be treated as confidential or covered under IP, patent, or NDA terms.", "No alterations or changes to the work without IUOVA''s consent during the project timeframe and validity period.", "Post-completion modifications will incur additional fees.", "IUOVA Design Company will transfer the Design Registration to the client for the selected concepts only."], "title": "Intellectual Property and Modifications"}, {"items": ["Iuova would like to publish some case study of the project for our brand development initiative.", "With approval from client would publish on its website and social media platforms.", "IUOVA would also do some video testimonials with client for the same."], "title": "Promotion and Portfolio"}, {"items": ["Bugs Fix type support will be provided from IUOVA for the deliverables associated with the project only for 30 days post handover."], "title": "Warranty"}], "gst": 18, "web": "www.iuovadesign.com", "acno": "005212100004508", "bank": "Bharat Co-Operative Bank Ltd.", "date": "23-06-2026", "faqs": [{"a": "A freelancer typically delivers one slice (just ID, or just CAD). A low-cost agency may deliver more slices but rarely with end-to-end accountability. IUOVA brings industrial design, engineering, electronics, prototyping, and manufacturing readiness under one roof, with a senior team that has shipped 200+ products to market. The cost difference reflects the difference between getting a design and getting a market-ready product platform — engineered for tooling, validated through prototyping, and supplier-aligned for manufacturing.", "q": "Why work with IUOVA over a freelancer or a cheaper agency?"}, {"a": "Our core team is 15–30 designers, engineers, and project managers across industrial design, mechanical engineering, electronics, and operations. For each engagement, we lock a named project team at kick-off — typically 4–6 people scaled to project complexity. We deliberately maintain a buffer of 20–25% spare capacity across the studio so urgent client requests don''t cascade into delays. Concurrent project load per senior team member is capped at 2–3 active engagements to ensure depth of attention. Timeline commitments are made only after capacity confirmation in kick-off.", "q": "What is your team size and how do you ensure capacity to deliver on time?"}, {"a": "Yes. While our Foundation/Growth/Flagship packages are designed as integrated workflows, individual phases can be engaged à la carte. Common à la carte engagements: ID-only sprint (2–3 weeks), engineering-only for clients with frozen ID (3–4 weeks), PCB development for mechanical-complete products (8–10 weeks). The proposal will quote your specific scope, and we will flag any handoff dependencies (e.g., engineering needs CAD-ready ID input). Pricing is published in our Custom Package templates.", "q": "Can we buy just industrial design, just engineering, or just electronics — without the full package?"}, {"a": "Industrial design: Adobe Creative Suite, Vizcom (AI rendering), KeyShot for visualization. Mechanical CAD: SolidWorks (primary), Fusion 360, NX for complex assemblies. Drawings: AutoCAD. Simulation: Ansys for FEA, basic CFD; SolidWorks Simulation for stress/thermal. Electronics: Altium Designer (primary PCB), KiCad for open-source projects, EasyEDA for rapid prototyping. Firmware: PlatformIO, ESP-IDF, STM32CubeIDE. Project management: Notion, Slack, Loom for async reviews. We deliver source files in industry-standard formats so the client is never locked to our specific tool stack.", "q": "What software and tools do you use for design and engineering?"}, {"a": "If cancellation happens within 7 days of signing AND before the kick-off meeting, we refund the 50% advance minus a 10% engagement fee that covers team reservation, contracting, and admin overhead. After kick-off has occurred, the engagement is considered live and standard milestone-based payment terms apply (the advance is non-refundable, but no further payments are due if the project is cancelled). Written cancellation notice is required in either case.", "q": "What if we sign the proposal but need to cancel before kick-off?"}, {"a": "Every phase has a defined Definition of Done documented in the proposal scope. At phase end, we hold a structured review where the client either signs off or flags issues. Any flagged issues are resolved within the included revision budget (3 rounds per phase). Sign-off is recorded via email confirmation or a signed phase completion certificate, which triggers the next milestone payment. Without sign-off, the project does not progress to the next phase — protecting both parties from scope drift and disputed deliverables.", "q": "What is the acceptance criteria — how is each phase signed off?"}, {"a": "Our public portfolio at iuovadesign.com is organized by category — consumer electronics, smart appliances, industrial products, wearables, and IoT devices. We have shipped products with Bajaj, Havells, Crompton, Siemens, Polycab, Panasonic, boAt, Godrej, L&T, Blue Star, and Prestige across these categories. For your specific category, we will share relevant case studies under NDA at the qualifying call. If we have not done your exact product before, we will be transparent about it and explain what adjacent expertise applies.", "q": "Have you worked on products in our specific category before?"}, {"a": "For Indian clients, all invoices include 18% GST as per current regulations. Our GSTIN is provided on the formal invoice. TDS, where applicable on professional services, can be deducted by the client and the certificate sent to us — we will reconcile against the final invoice. International clients receive a USD-denominated invoice with no GST, suitable for foreign exchange payment via SWIFT. Invoices are issued at the start of each milestone (advance, Phase 1 sign-off, handover) and are payable within 7 working days.", "q": "How is GST treated, and what is your invoice format?"}, {"a": "For 30 days post-handover, we provide free corrective work for any defect directly traceable to our deliverables — design errors, drawing mistakes, missing specifications, etc. Beyond this period, our maximum liability is capped at the total fees paid for the engagement, in line with standard product design industry contracts. We carry professional indemnity insurance covering the work product. We do not bear liability for third-party manufacturing defects, vendor errors, end-user misuse, or downstream product market performance.", "q": "What is your warranty and liability cap on delivered designs?"}, {"a": "Yes — many of our engagements are confidential by design, particularly for startup clients in stealth mode or established brands launching disruptive products. We sign mutual NDAs before any technical details are shared, restrict project access to a named core team, segment file storage from the rest of our infrastructure, and contractually exclude the project from our public portfolio (or include it only after public launch with permission). For exceptional secrecy needs, we can offer code-named project tracking and escrow-based deliverable handover.", "q": "Can you work under deep secrecy on stealth-mode products?"}], "ifsc": "BCBM0000053", "logo": "/assets/holder_logo-CW7spHUh.png", "refs": "Crompton\nPolycab\nYash Fans\nBajaj Electricals\nNational Plastics\nDover Brookes\nHelpmesee\nMyro\nPrestige\nPreethi\nBoat", "about": "Iuova Design Company is an Award-winning Product Innovation Partner, providing end to end Product Development Solutions.\n\nOver the years, We have developed more than 200 Products in categories such as – Home & Kitchen Appliances, Consumer Electronics, Medical Devices, Home Automation, Metal Enclosures and many more.", "email": "info@iuova.in", "logos": [{"img": "", "name": "Bajaj Electricals"}, {"img": "", "name": "Havells"}, {"img": "", "name": "Crompton"}, {"img": "", "name": "Siemens"}, {"img": "", "name": "Polycab"}, {"img": "", "name": "Panasonic"}, {"img": "", "name": "boAt"}, {"img": "", "name": "Godrej"}, {"img": "", "name": "L&T"}, {"img": "", "name": "Blue Star"}, {"img": "", "name": "Prestige"}, {"img": "", "name": "Yash Fans"}], "phone": "9819918315", "risks": [{"risk": "Tooling vendor capacity delays during festival/year-end periods", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Pre-aligned vendor pool with 3 alternates; tooling slot booked at design-freeze stage, not at handover.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Component obsolescence in embedded BOM (semiconductors)", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Phase 3 BOM uses parts with minimum 5-year lifecycle commitment from manufacturers; second-source identified for >80% of critical components.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Regulatory certification timeline (BIS / EMC / FCC)", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Compliance touchpoints embedded in design phase, not deferred to post-prototype. Test lab slots reserved at Phase 2 sign-off.", "probability": "Low"}, {"risk": "Late client-side feedback creating design freeze drift", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Stage-gate calendar fixed in kick-off; delays beyond 7 working days trigger documented schedule renegotiation per Section 4 of T&C.", "probability": "High"}], "swift": "BCMLINBB", "acname": "IUOVA", "branch": "Mulund (West)", "client": "Mersiv Labs LLP", "remark": "Not agreeing to IP condition and out of budget", "result": "A production-cleared, manufacturing-ready product platform — engineered for seamless tooling, vendor alignment, and scalable commercialization.", "address": "Office No 504, 5th Floor,\nFilix Tower, Mulund West,\nMumbai – 400078, Maharashtra", "concern": "Eshaan Mehta", "project": "Blob", "v1_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bcyXyAHh-P_M8MzZYUycJGC6e3C-mMmy/view", "v2_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Ln5IMV4P5jMzIQtEIBnAWjuFt5JfF77/view", "feedback": "", "outcomes": [{"body": "Curated design directions with refined CMF options and high-quality visualizations, supported by clear engineering rationale.", "title": "Industrial Design & CMF Package"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade 3D data optimized for tooling, scalability, and seamless production integration.", "title": "Tooling-Ready CAD Release"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade PCB and Gerber files. Optimized for scalability and seamless production integration.", "title": "Production Ready Electronics"}, {"body": "Precision-built prototype for real-world validation of form, fit, and performance.", "title": "Functional Prototype (As per scope)"}, {"body": "Comprehensive technical documentation validating manufacturability, performance, and risk mitigation.", "title": "Engineering & Validation Reports (As per scope)"}], "packages": [{"id": "pkg_zqrnu65", "label": "Foundation Package", "phases": [{"inr": "225000", "name": "Phase 1 - Industrial Design + CMF with Schematics", "weeks": "2", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Kick off meeting & brief discussion", "Brainstorming & Ideation on schematic", "Client review & refinement of schematic", "Concept 3D models", "Concept Renders", "ID presentation", "Client review & ID Refinement", "Final Presentation"], "deliverables": "1) Design review & validation.\n2) 3 CMF combinations for selected concept."}, {"inr": "As per actual", "name": "Phase 1.1 – Alpha Prototype", "weeks": "As per actual", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "1) One Visual prototype of selected concept."}, {"inr": "380000", "name": "Phase 2 - Product Engineering & Prototyping", "weeks": "4", "enabled": true, "activities": ["3D CAD models", "Review, update CAD files", "Engineering review & Updated CAD files", "File submission for prototyping/mold maker''s review", "Updated CAD files based on prototype/mold maker''s feedback", "Internal review & Engineering refinement", "Value Engineering", "Final submission"], "deliverables": "1) Engineering 3D CAD file of one selected concept''s components & Assembly based on final prototype. (Step or Parasolid)"}, {"inr": "As per Actual", "name": "Phase