IUOVA''s drawing format)\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 2.2 – Beta Prototype\",\"weeks\":\"-\",\"inr\":\"As per Actual\",\"activities\":[],\"deliverables\":\"1) Functional/Near real Prototype as per approved materials.\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 3 - Electrical & Electronics Development\",\"weeks\":\"12\",\"inr\":850000,\"activities\":[\"Identify the components\",\"PCB architecture\",\"PCB design\",\"Review & refinements\",\"Final PCB design submission\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) Embedded Hardware (Bill Of Materials)\\n2) Embedded Software (Gerber File)\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 3.1 – PCB Prototype\",\"weeks\":\"Included\",\"inr\":\"Included\",\"activities\":[],\"deliverables\":\"1) One Prototype of PCB for POC.\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 4 - Product Validation\",\"weeks\":\"3\",\"inr\":200000,\"activities\":[\"Load test/stress analysis\",\"Drop test\",\"Thermal analysis\",\"FEA simulation\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) One report of CFD Analysis (2 Iterations).\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 5 – Manufacturing Readiness, Vendor Development & Sourcing\",\"weeks\":\"3\",\"inr\":200000,\"activities\":[\"Vendor development\",\"Tool development\",\"Batch production\",\"Component Sourcing\"],\"deliverables\":\"-\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Additional Phase 6 - Product Strategy, 360 Research Architecture\",\"weeks\":\"-\",\"inr\":\"-\",\"activities\":[\"Online & Offline survey\",\"Client study\",\"E-commerce study\",\"Area of opportunities as per survey\",\"Geographic study\",\"CMF study\",\"Threshold\"],\"deliverables\":\"-\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 7 - Packaging Development\",\"weeks\":\"2\",\"inr\":120000,\"activities\":[\"Packaging design development \",\"Product placement and protection approach\",\"Packaging graphics & product communication\",\"Material & finish selection\",\"Packaging refinement & finalisation\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) Final packaging design\\n2) 3D packaging visualisation using existing product CAD\\n3) Packaging specification sheet (material, finish & dimensions)\\n4) Final vendor handover files\",\"enabled\":true}],\"paymentSummary\":[\"50% Advance, 30% against Phase 1 and 20% against Project handover.\",\"Cost of all Prototyping is extra as per applicable.\",\"Quote is inclusive of all taxes.\",\"Any additions or changes to the Scope of Work (SOW) after finalizing the design or beyond three iterations will incur additional charges as applicable.\"],\"timeline\":\"29-30 Weeks from Commencement of Project.\",\"deliverablesNote\":\"As per above mentioned.\",\"bankDetailsNote\":\"See \\\"Project Investment & Banking\\\" page for full wire transfer details.\",\"outOfScope\":[\"Mass production tooling, mold making, and tool fabrication costs\",\"Regulatory certifications (BIS, EMC, FCC, CE) — quoted separately\",\"IP filings, design registration government fees, and trademark prosecution\",\"Post-launch warranty support beyond 30 days from handover\"],\"successMetrics\":[{\"metric\":\"Design freeze achieved within Phase 1 timeline\",\"target\":\"4 weeks from kick-off\"},{\"metric\":\"CAD files reviewed and signed off by tooling partner\",\"target\":\"≥ 1 vendor sign-off\"},{\"metric\":\"Prototype passes agreed-upon test plan\",\"target\":\"≥ 90% pass rate\"},{\"metric\":\"Final BOM cost variance vs. quoted target\",\"target\":\"≤ 5% deviation\"}]}"}', 0, 'Draft', '{"fx": 90, "tc": [{"items": ["The Client shall provide complete and detailed information before project commencement to ensure accurate delivery."], "title": "Project Initiation"}, {"items": ["Client must make payments as per payment schedule in agreement, delay in payments more that 30 days will incur additional delay charges of 5% of total fees and work will be halted. It will commence once payments are cleared.", "Invoicing need to complete within 7 days of milestone completion.", "Travelling will be billed as per actual for onsite client or vendor visits."], "title": "Payment Terms"}, {"items": ["We will provide fair concepts based on client inputs and feedback.", "Clients are allowed up to three revisions; additional revisions will incur extra charges as mutually agreed.", "Modifications after finalizing the design and CAD files will be treated as additional scope of work and will incur additional charges as mutually agreed."], "title": "Concept Development and Revisions"}, {"items": ["Client-induced delays exceeding 2 months will incur waiting charges of 10% of the total fees per delayed week.", "Client must make complete payment once the services are delivered by IUOVA, till that ownership of the developed Design/Product associated with the project remains with IUOVA."], "title": "Delays and Waiting Charges"}, {"items": ["Work outside the original scope of work will be charged based on the quantum of work or a mutually agreed value."], "title": "Additional Work"}, {"items": ["Mutual consent is required for project cancellation.", "Client-initiated cancellations: advance payments are non-refundable.", "IUOVA-initiated cancellations (due to client fault): client must clear payments for work done."], "title": "Project Cancellation"}, {"items": ["Any information that is publicly available will not be treated as confidential or covered under IP, patent, or NDA terms.", "No alterations or changes to the work without IUOVA''s consent during the project timeframe and validity period.", "Post-completion modifications will incur additional fees.", "IUOVA Design Company will transfer the Design Registration to the client for the selected concepts only."], "title": "Intellectual Property and Modifications"}, {"items": ["Iuova would like to publish some case study of the project for our brand development initiative.", "With approval from client would publish on its website and social media platforms.", "IUOVA would also do some video testimonials with client for the same."], "title": "Promotion and Portfolio"}, {"items": ["Bugs Fix type support will be provided from IUOVA for the deliverables associated with the project only for 30 days post handover."], "title": "Warranty"}], "gst": 18, "rfq": {"id": "66c96f20-adbc-4ce6-9b32-f904403524eb", "budget": "5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)", "services": ["Product Design Services (Industrial Design)", "Manufacturing Services", "Prototyping Services"], "timeline": "1 - 2 months", "company_info": "We are trying to develop innovative dental devices for the betterment of patients. ", "business_size": "0 - 10 Crores INR", "hear_about_us": "Google", "project_scope": "We want to develop above products with its accessories. You can check Hanau Wide Vue articulator and a Slidematic facebow online. These are the established products in the market. We need to make similar products with changes and to get a patent on this. I need to know approximate time and cost for the same.", "has_components": false, "form_experience": 5, "has_manufacturing": false, "manufacturing_moq": "1000", "additional_details": "Please check both above mentioned products online.", "components_details": "", "important_features": "Technology Overview\nIndia, as a developing country with a large population of dental students and practitioners, requires cost-effective alternatives to the expensive articulators currently available in the market. The high cost of imported and premium articulator systems often limits their accessibility, particularly in undergraduate institutions, postgraduate training programs, and private clinical practice. Consequently, there is a pressing need for an affordable articulator that can be widely adopted without imposing a significant financial burden on users.\nHowever, affordability should not come at the expense of quality or clinical performance. An ideal articulator for the Indian market should be robust, precisely engineered, and capable of accurately reproducing mandibular movements to ensure reliable diagnosis, treatment planning, and prosthesis fabrication. By combining advanced design features with economical manufacturing, such an articulator would bridge the gap between cost and functionality, making high-quality prosthodontic care and education more accessible while promoting better clinical outcomes.\n\n* Describe the problem and existing alternate solutions (in terms of features and/or\naffordability). 248-250 words)\nRoutinely used articulators possess several design limitations that may reduce the accuracy of mandibular movement simulation. A major drawback is the non-adjustable intercondylar distance, which does not account for individual anatomical variations. As a result, the articulator may fail to reproduce the true position of the condyles, potentially leading to occlusal discrepancies and interferences during prosthodontic procedures.\nAnother limitation is the presence of negative graduations in the horizontal condylar guidance (HCG) slot. Since HCG values are not negative in patients, these markings are clinically unnecessary and often create confusion among students and practitioners during articulator programming.\nThe conventional straight and rigid incisal guide pin also presents difficulties when the vertical dimension is increased. Raising the vertical dimension alters the contact point of the incisal pin, making it difficult to maintain a consistent reference and complicating occlusal adjustments.\nIn addition, many articulators allow lateral condylar guidance (LCG) adjustment only up to 15°, whereas studies have reported values of up to 40° - 60° in some patients. This restricted range limits accurate replication of mandibular movements in such cases.\nThe proposed new articulator aims to overcome these shortcomings by incorporating an adjustable intercondylar distance, eliminating unnecessary negative HCG markings, improving the incisal guide pin design to maintain a stable reference during changes in vertical dimension, and extending the LCG adjustment range to better accommodate individual patient variations.\n", "require_manufacturing": true}, "web": "www.iuovadesign.com", "acno": "005212100004508", "bank": "Bharat Co-Operative Bank Ltd.", "date": "16-07-2026", "faqs": [{"a": "A freelancer typically delivers one slice (just ID, or just CAD). A low-cost agency may deliver more slices but rarely with end-to-end accountability. IUOVA brings industrial design, engineering, electronics, prototyping, and manufacturing readiness under one roof, with a senior team that has shipped 200+ products to market. The cost difference reflects the difference between getting a design and getting a market-ready product platform — engineered for tooling, validated through prototyping, and supplier-aligned for manufacturing.", "q": "Why work with IUOVA over a freelancer or a cheaper agency?"}, {"a": "Our core team is 15–30 designers, engineers, and project managers across industrial design, mechanical engineering, electronics, and operations. For each engagement, we lock a named project team at kick-off — typically 4–6 people scaled to project complexity. We deliberately maintain a buffer of 20–25% spare capacity across the studio so urgent client requests don''t cascade into delays. Concurrent project load per senior team member is capped at 2–3 active engagements to ensure depth of attention. Timeline commitments are made only after capacity confirmation in kick-off.", "q": "What is your team size and how do you ensure capacity to deliver on time?"}, {"a": "Yes. While our Foundation/Growth/Flagship packages are designed as integrated workflows, individual phases can be engaged à la carte. Common à la carte engagements: ID-only sprint (2–3 weeks), engineering-only for clients with frozen ID (3–4 weeks), PCB development for mechanical-complete products (8–10 weeks). The proposal will quote your specific scope, and we will flag any handoff dependencies (e.g., engineering needs CAD-ready ID input). Pricing is published in our Custom Package templates.", "q": "Can we buy just industrial design, just engineering, or just electronics — without the full package?"}, {"a": "Industrial design: Adobe Creative Suite, Vizcom (AI rendering), KeyShot for visualization. Mechanical CAD: SolidWorks (primary), Fusion 360, NX for complex assemblies. Drawings: AutoCAD. Simulation: Ansys for FEA, basic CFD; SolidWorks Simulation for stress/thermal. Electronics: Altium Designer (primary PCB), KiCad for open-source projects, EasyEDA for rapid prototyping. Firmware: PlatformIO, ESP-IDF, STM32CubeIDE. Project management: Notion, Slack, Loom for async reviews. We deliver source files in industry-standard formats so the client is never locked to our specific tool stack.", "q": "What software and tools do you use for design and engineering?"}, {"a": "If cancellation happens within 7 days of signing AND before the kick-off meeting, we refund the 50% advance minus a 10% engagement fee that covers team reservation, contracting, and admin overhead. After kick-off has occurred, the engagement is considered live and standard milestone-based payment terms apply (the advance is non-refundable, but no further payments are due if the project is cancelled). Written cancellation notice is required in either case.", "q": "What if we sign the proposal but need to cancel before kick-off?"}, {"a": "Every phase has a defined Definition of Done documented in the proposal scope. At phase end, we hold a structured review where the client either signs off or flags issues. Any flagged issues are resolved within the included revision budget (3 rounds per phase). Sign-off is recorded via email confirmation or a signed phase completion certificate, which triggers the next milestone payment. Without sign-off, the project does not progress to the next phase — protecting both parties from scope drift and disputed deliverables.", "q": "What is the acceptance criteria — how is each phase signed off?"}, {"a": "Our public portfolio at iuovadesign.com is organized by category — consumer electronics, smart appliances, industrial products, wearables, and IoT devices. We have shipped products with Bajaj, Havells, Crompton, Siemens, Polycab, Panasonic, boAt, Godrej, L&T, Blue Star, and Prestige across these categories. For your specific category, we will share relevant case studies under NDA at the qualifying call. If we have not done your exact product before, we will be transparent about it and explain what adjacent expertise applies.", "q": "Have you worked on products in our specific category before?"}, {"a": "For Indian clients, all invoices include 18% GST as per current regulations. Our GSTIN is provided on the formal invoice. TDS, where applicable on professional services, can be deducted by the client and the certificate sent to us — we will reconcile against the final invoice. International clients receive a USD-denominated invoice with no GST, suitable for foreign exchange payment via SWIFT. Invoices are issued at the start of each milestone (advance, Phase 1 sign-off, handover) and are payable within 7 working days.", "q": "How is GST treated, and what is your invoice format?"}, {"a": "For 30 days post-handover, we provide free corrective work for any defect directly traceable to our deliverables — design errors, drawing mistakes, missing specifications, etc. Beyond this period, our maximum liability is capped at the total fees paid for the engagement, in line with standard product design industry contracts. We carry professional indemnity insurance covering the work product. We do not bear liability for third-party manufacturing defects, vendor errors, end-user misuse, or downstream product market performance.", "q": "What is your warranty and liability cap on delivered designs?"}, {"a": "Yes — many of our engagements are confidential by design, particularly for startup clients in stealth mode or established brands launching disruptive products. We sign mutual NDAs before any technical details are shared, restrict project access to a named core team, segment file storage from the rest of our infrastructure, and contractually exclude the project from our public portfolio (or include it only after public launch with permission). For exceptional secrecy needs, we can offer code-named project tracking and escrow-based deliverable handover.", "q": "Can you work under deep secrecy on stealth-mode products?"}, {"a": "Yes — many of our engagements are confidential by design, particularly for startup clients in stealth mode or established brands launching disruptive products. We sign mutual NDAs before any technical details are shared, restrict project access to a named core team, segment file storage from the rest of our infrastructure, and contractually exclude the project from our public portfolio (or include it only after public launch with permission). For exceptional secrecy needs, we can offer code-named project tracking and escrow-based deliverable handover.", "q": "Can you work under deep secrecy on stealth-mode products?"}, {"a": "Discounts for additional concepts apply only to the design phase, not the overall project. One extra concept beyond your primary selection is offered at 50% of the base concept fee. If you purchase a total of three concepts, the two additional concepts are charged at 40% of the base concept fee. All discounts apply only to the design phase cost.", "q": " What if we want to purchase more than one design concept?"}, {"a": "Yes — we can run multiple projects subject to project-team availability and scheduling. When you engage us on two concurrent projects, we include one complimentary secondary package (scope and delivery terms to be defined in the proposal). Final scheduling, resource allocation, and exact deliverables will be confirmed during scoping.", "q": "Can we run two projects with you at the same time?"}, {"a": "There are no additional design charges for creating size variants of a selected concept. Costs for size versions are limited to engineering, prototyping, testing, tooling (if applicable), and other development activities, which will be charged per our standard engineering and prototype pricing. Final costs are scoped and confirmed after an initial review to determine the required engineering effort for each size variant.", "q": "If we want the same selected design language but different size versions of the product, how is costing handled?"}], "ifsc": "BCBM0000053", "logo": "/assets/holder_logo-CW7spHUh.png", "refs": "Crompton\nPolycab\nYash Fans\nBajaj Electricals\nNational Plastics\nDover Brookes\nHelpmesee\nMyro\nPrestige\nPreethi\nBoat", "about": "Iuova Design Company is an Award-winning Product Innovation Partner, providing end to end Product Development Solutions.\n\nOver the years, We have developed more than 200 Products in categories such as – Home & Kitchen Appliances, Consumer Electronics, Medical Devices, Home Automation, Metal Enclosures and many more.", "email": "info@iuova.in", "logos": [{"img": "", "name": "Bajaj Electricals"}, {"img": "", "name": "Havells"}, {"img": "", "name": "Crompton"}, {"img": "", "name": "Siemens"}, {"img": "", "name": "Polycab"}, {"img": "", "name": "Panasonic"}, {"img": "", "name": "boAt"}, {"img": "", "name": "Godrej"}, {"img": "", "name": "L&T"}, {"img": "", "name": "Blue Star"}, {"img": "", "name": "Prestige"}, {"img": "", "name": "Yash Fans"}], "phone": "09370015510", "risks": [{"risk": "Tooling vendor capacity delays during festival/year-end periods", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Pre-aligned vendor pool with 3 alternates; tooling slot booked at design-freeze stage, not at handover.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Component obsolescence in embedded BOM (semiconductors)", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Phase 3 BOM uses parts with minimum 5-year lifecycle commitment from manufacturers; second-source identified for >80% of critical components.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Regulatory certification timeline (BIS / EMC / FCC)", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Compliance touchpoints embedded 