ing is extra as per applicable.\",\"Quote is inclusive of all taxes.\",\"Any additions or changes to the Scope of Work (SOW) after finalizing the design or beyond three iterations will incur additional charges as applicable.\"],\"timeline\":\"29-30 Weeks from Commencement of Project.\",\"deliverablesNote\":\"As per above mentioned.\",\"bankDetailsNote\":\"See \\\"Project Investment & Banking\\\" page for full wire transfer details.\",\"outOfScope\":[\"Mass production tooling, mold making, and tool fabrication costs\",\"Regulatory certifications (BIS, EMC, FCC, CE) — quoted separately\",\"IP filings, design registration government fees, and trademark prosecution\",\"Post-launch warranty support beyond 30 days from handover\"],\"successMetrics\":[{\"metric\":\"Design freeze achieved within Phase 1 timeline\",\"target\":\"4 weeks from kick-off\"},{\"metric\":\"CAD files reviewed and signed off by tooling partner\",\"target\":\"≥ 1 vendor sign-off\"},{\"metric\":\"Prototype passes agreed-upon test plan\",\"target\":\"≥ 90% pass rate\"},{\"metric\":\"Final BOM cost variance vs. quoted target\",\"target\":\"≤ 5% deviation\"}]}"}', 0, 'Draft', '{"fx": 90, "tc": [{"items": ["The Client shall provide complete and detailed information before project commencement to ensure accurate delivery."], "title": "Project Initiation"}, {"items": ["Client must make payments as per payment schedule in agreement, delay in payments more that 30 days will incur additional delay charges of 5% of total fees and work will be halted. It will commence once payments are cleared.", "Invoicing need to complete within 7 days of milestone completion.", "Travelling will be billed as per actual for onsite client or vendor visits."], "title": "Payment Terms"}, {"items": ["We will provide fair concepts based on client inputs and feedback.", "Clients are allowed up to three revisions; additional revisions will incur extra charges as mutually agreed.", "Modifications after finalizing the design and CAD files will be treated as additional scope of work and will incur additional charges as mutually agreed."], "title": "Concept Development and Revisions"}, {"items": ["Client-induced delays exceeding 2 months will incur waiting charges of 10% of the total fees per delayed week.", "Client must make complete payment once the services are delivered by IUOVA, till that ownership of the developed Design/Product associated with the project remains with IUOVA."], "title": "Delays and Waiting Charges"}, {"items": ["Work outside the original scope of work will be charged based on the quantum of work or a mutually agreed value."], "title": "Additional Work"}, {"items": ["Mutual consent is required for project cancellation.", "Client-initiated cancellations: advance payments are non-refundable.", "IUOVA-initiated cancellations (due to client fault): client must clear payments for work done."], "title": "Project Cancellation"}, {"items": ["Any information that is publicly available will not be treated as confidential or covered under IP, patent, or NDA terms.", "No alterations or changes to the work without IUOVA''s consent during the project timeframe and validity period.", "Post-completion modifications will incur additional fees.", "IUOVA Design Company will transfer the Design Registration to the client for the selected concepts only."], "title": "Intellectual Property and Modifications"}, {"items": ["Iuova would like to publish some case study of the project for our brand development initiative.", "With approval from client would publish on its website and social media platforms.", "IUOVA would also do some video testimonials with client for the same."], "title": "Promotion and Portfolio"}, {"items": ["Bugs Fix type support will be provided from IUOVA for the deliverables associated with the project only for 30 days post handover."], "title": "Warranty"}], "gst": 18, "rfq": {"id": "9ef7db4b-fc4c-4cd3-8813-c20a13af7513", "budget": "15 - 25 Lakhs (Upto 25000 USD)", "services": ["Industrial Design Services, Prototyping & Model Making Services, Manufacturing Readiness Services"], "timeline": "3 -4 months", "company_info": "Srahi is a hardware-led AI companion ecosystem specifically designed for the \"Urban Silver\" market. We provide a proactive, touch-first assistant that manages the daily routines and emotional connectivity of independent elders while offering quantified peace of mind to their families. Our business operates on a \"hardware-light, software-margin\" model, where an ergonomic physical device serves as the primary gateway for a high-trust platform of integrated services.", "business_size": "0 -10 Crores INR", "hear_about_us": "Google", "project_scope": "The product is an AI-enabled wearable pendant, internally referred to as the \"Pebble,\" designed to act as a proactive companion for the Indian elderly market. Unlike reactive medical alert systems, Srahi is an \"always-on\" luxury butler that facilitates daily routines, emotional support, and vernacular communication.\nProduct Definition\n• Form Factor: A sleek, ergonomic wearable (Pebble aesthetic) designed for high tactile comfort.\n• Core Hardware: Based on the ESP32-S3 chipset, utilizing a BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy) bridge to offload 90% of heavy processing to a tethered smartphone.\n• Primary User Interface: Voice-first and touch-responsive, optimized for \"Hinglish\" and regional Indian dialects (Marathi, Tamil, Kannada).\nScope of Work (SOW)\nThe scope is divided into three critical tracks to ensure the product is production-ready within the target price point:\n1. Industrial Design & Ergonomics\n• Conceptualization: Developing the physical \"Pebble\" form factor that emphasizes dignity over medical surveillance.\n• Prototyping: Creation of functional prototypes to test weight, tactile response, and wearable attachment points (neck/pocket).\n2. Design for Manufacturing (DFM)\n• BOM Optimization: Finalizing the Bill of Materials to lock in a ₹1,999 target cost at scale.\n• Tooling & Molds: Engineering high-precision mold development for the outer casing and internal component housing.\n• Regulatory Compliance: Ensuring the design meets BIS and WPC certification standards for Indian electronics.\n3. Systems Integration\n• Firmware Development: Optimizing the ESP32-S3 for battery efficiency and stable BLE connectivity.\n• AI Pipeline: Integration of the on-device wake-word engine with our proprietary cloud-based Personalized RAG (Memory) layer.\n\n", "has_components": true, "form_experience": 2, "has_manufacturing": false, "manufacturing_moq": "2000", "additional_details": "To ensure a successful partnership and maintain our target timeline, we require clarity on the following execution-level details:\n1. Cost Management & DFM Expertise\n• BOM Governance: How does your team approach Design for Manufacturing (DFM) to ensure the hardware doesn''t exceed our ₹1,999 target cost while maintaining a premium \"Pebble\" feel? \n• Vendor Ecosystem: Do you have existing relationships with Tier-1 EMS partners (e.g., in Noida or Chennai) to streamline the transition from prototyping to the first 2,000-unit production run? \n2. Technical & Regulatory Integration\n• Connectivity Optimization: What is your experience in optimizing ESP32-S3 and BLE stability to ensure the \"Phone-Tether\" connection remains reliable without excessive battery drain? \n• Certification Support: Will your scope include the technical documentation and design iterations required for BIS and WPC certifications? \n3. Geriatric UX & Reliability\n• Testing for Seniors: What is your methodology for testing tactile ergonomics and voice interface responsiveness specifically for the elderly demographic? \n• Durability & Safety: Since this is a wearable for seniors, what are your standards for drop-testing, sweat resistance, and hypoallergenic material selection for the casing? \n4. Timeline & Milestones\n• Phased Delivery: Can you provide a breakdown of your internal milestones to align with our 15–18 month runway, specifically targeting the delivery of production-ready moulds within the first two quarters? \n\n", "components_details": "While we are looking for the design vendor to lead the overall industrial and mechanical integration, the core of the Srahi hardware architecture is predefined based on our strategic roadmap to ensure we maintain a ₹1,999 BOM target.\nWe will specify or provide the following core components and architectural constraints:\n• Chipset Platform: The device could be built on the ESP32-S3 base.\n• Connectivity Architecture: The hardware must function as a smartphone peripheral, utilizing a BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy) bridge to offload 90% of processing tasks to the mobile application.\n• AI Infrastructure: We provide the proprietary RAG-based memory systems and fine-tuned vernacular voice models for Marathi, Tamil, and Kannada that reside in our secure cloud/app layer.\n• Strategic Oversight: We will provide a dedicated Manufacturing/Hardware Lead as a consultant to manage factory relations and oversee the Bill of Materials (BOM).\n• UX Framework: We provide the clinical and geriatric logic for the \"Butler\" personality and safety layers, vetted by our Geriatric UX/Clinical Consultant.\n", "important_features": "The most important features of the Srahi \"Pebble\" are centered on moving away from a \"medical tracking\" feel toward a high-utility, respectful AI Butler experience. The primary requirements include:\n1. Core Interaction & AI Intelligence\n• Vernacular Voice First: The device must natively handle \"Hinglish\" and code-switching between English and regional dialects like Marathi, Tamil, and Kannada.\n• Proprietary RAG Memory Layer: A secure, personal memory vault that allows the AI to remember past conversations, routines, and preferences, making the interaction deeply personalized over time.\n• Proactive Companionship: Beyond reactive commands, the AI must initiate respectful prompts for \"yoga time,\" medication reminders, or hydration.\n2. Hardware & Industrial Design\n• \"Pebble\" Aesthetic: A focus on high-quality industrial design that prioritizes ergonomics and dignity, ensuring the senior feels they are wearing a premium accessory rather than a surveillance tag. Primary Interface: Voice-first with a tactile,\nyes/no switch—simple, familiar, and easy to use\n• Optimized Connectivity: A stable BLE (Bluetooth Low Energy) bridge to a tethered smartphone, offloading 90% of heavy processing to maintain battery life and device lightness.\n• Long Battery Life: The hardware must be optimized so that the wake-word engine and connectivity do not deplete the battery in a few hours.\n3. Safety & Reliability\n• Non-Alarming Health Alerts: A clinical-grade SOS and health-alert logic that is medically sound but communicated in a respectful, non-alarming tone.\n• Trust & Compliance: Data residency compliance and necessary certifications (BIS/WPC) to ensure the platform is secure and reliable for the Indian market.\n\n", "require_manufacturing": true}, "web": "www.iuovadesign.com", "acno": "005212100004508", "bank": "Bharat Co-Operative Bank Ltd.", "date": "22-04-2026", "faqs": [{"a": "A freelancer typically delivers one slice (just ID, or just CAD). A low-cost agency may deliver more slices but rarely with end-to-end accountability. IUOVA brings industrial design, engineering, electronics, prototyping, and manufacturing readiness under one roof, with a senior team that has shipped 200+ products to market. The cost difference reflects the difference between getting a design and getting a market-ready product platform — engineered for tooling, validated through prototyping, and supplier-aligned for manufacturing.", "q": "Why work with IUOVA over a freelancer or a cheaper agency?"}, {"a": "Our core team is 15–30 designers, engineers, and project managers across industrial design, mechanical engineering, electronics, and operations. For each engagement, we lock a named project team at kick-off — typically 4–6 people scaled to project complexity. We deliberately maintain a buffer of 20–25% spare capacity across the studio so urgent client requests don''t cascade into delays. Concurrent project load per senior team member is capped at 2–3 active engagements to ensure depth of attention. Timeline commitments are made only after capacity confirmation in kick-off.", "q": "What is your team size and how do you ensure capacity to deliver on time?"}, {"a": "Yes. While our Foundation/Growth/Flagship packages are designed as integrated workflows, individual phases can be engaged à la carte. Common à la carte engagements: ID-only sprint (2–3 weeks), engineering-only for clients with frozen ID (3–4 weeks), PCB development for mechanical-complete products (8–10 weeks). The proposal will quote your specific scope, and we will flag any handoff dependencies (e.g., engineering needs CAD-ready ID input). Pricing is published in our Custom Package templates.", "q": "Can we buy just industrial design, just engineering, or just electronics — without the full package?"}, {"a": "Industrial design: Adobe Creative Suite, Vizcom (AI rendering), KeyShot for visualization. Mechanical CAD: SolidWorks (primary), Fusion 360, NX for complex assemblies. Drawings: AutoCAD. Simulation: Ansys for FEA, basic CFD; SolidWorks Simulation for stress/thermal. Electronics: Altium Designer (primary PCB), KiCad for open-source projects, EasyEDA for rapid prototyping. Firmware: PlatformIO, ESP-IDF, STM32CubeIDE. Project management: Notion, Slack, Loom for async reviews. We deliver source files in industry-standard formats so the client is never locked to our specific tool stack.", "q": "What software and tools do you use for design and engineering?"}, {"a": "If cancellation happens within 7 days of signing AND before the kick-off meeting, we refund the 50% advance minus a 10% engagement fee that covers team reservation, contracting, and admin overhead. After kick-off has occurred, the engagement is considered live and standard milestone-based payment terms apply (the advance is non-refundable, but no further payments are due if the project is cancelled). Written cancellation notice is required in either case.", "q": "What if we sign the proposal but need to cancel before kick-off?"}, {"a": "Every phase has a defined Definition of Done documented in the proposal scope. At phase end, we hold a structured review where the client either signs off or flags issues. Any flagged issues are resolved within the included revision budget (3 rounds per phase). Sign-off is recorded via email confirmation or a signed phase completion certificate, which triggers the next milestone payment. Without sign-off, the project does not progress to the next phase — protecting both parties from scope drift and disputed deliverables.", "q": "What is the acceptance criteria — how is each phase signed off?"}, {"a": "Our development framework is specifically designed to mitigate this risk through a structured, stage-gated process. We incorporate client validation checkpoints at each critical phase—ideation, sketch development, and concept presentation—ensuring alignment on design direction before progressing further. In the event that the proposed concepts do not meet expectations, we initiate a controlled second iteration cycle within the ideation phase. This allows us to recalibrate design direction based on structured feedback while maintaining overall project timelines. Such scenarios are rare due to our continuous validation approach, but the process is built to accommodate them as a defined fallback.", "q": "What if we don''t like the design concepts presented?"}, {"a": "Our public portfolio at iuovadesign.com is organized by category — consumer electronics, smart appliances, industrial products, wearables, and IoT devices. We have shipped products with Bajaj, Havells, Crompton, Siemens, Polycab, Panasonic, boAt, Godrej, L&T, Blue Star, and Prestige across these categories. For your specific category, we will share relevant case studies under NDA at the qualifying call. If we have not done your exact product before, we will be transparent about it and explain what adjacent expertise applies.", "q": "Have you worked on products in our specific category before?"}, {"a": "For Indian clients, all invoices include 18% GST as per current regulations. Our GSTIN is provided on the formal invoice. TDS, where applicable on professional services, can be deducted by the client and the certificate sent to us — we will reconcile against the final invoice. International clients receive a USD-denominated invoice with no GST, suitable for foreign exchange payment via SWIFT. Invoices are issued at the start of each milestone (advance, Phase 1 sign-off, handover) and are payable within 7 working days.", "q": "How is GST treated, and what is your invoice format?"}, {"a": "For 30 days post-handover, we provide free corrective work for any defect directly traceable to our deliverables — design errors, drawing mistakes, missing specifications, etc. Beyond this period, our maximum liability is capped at the total fees paid for the engagement, in line with standard product design industry contracts. We carry professional indemnity insurance covering the work product. We do not bear liability for third-party manufacturing defects, vendor errors, end-user misuse, or downstream product market performance.", "q": "What is your warranty and liability cap on delivered designs?"}, {"a": "Yes — many of our engagements are confidential by design, particularly for startup clients in stealth mode or established brands launching disruptive products. We sign mutual NDAs before any technical details are shared, restrict project access to a named core team, segment file storage from the rest of our infrastructure, and contractually exclude the project from our public portfolio (or include it only after public launch with permission). For exceptional secrecy needs, we can offer code-named project tracking and escrow-based deliverable handover.", "q": "Can you work under deep secrecy on stealth-mode products?"}], "ifsc": "BCBM0000053", "logo": "/assets/holder_logo-CW7spHUh.png", "refs": "Crompton\nPolycab\nYash Fans\nBajaj Electricals\nNational Plastics\nDover Brookes\nHelpmesee\nMyro\nPrestige\nPreethi\nBoat", "about": "Iuova Design Company is an Award-winning Product Innovation Partner, providing end to end Product Development Solutions.\n\nOver the years, We have developed more than 200 Products in categories such as – Home & Kitchen Appliances, Consumer Electronics, Medical Devices, Home Automation, Metal Enclosures and many more.", "email": "info@iuova.in", "logos": [{"img": "", "name": "Bajaj Electricals"}, {"img": "", "name": "Havells"}, {"img": "", "name": "Crompton"}, {"img": "", "name": "Siemens"}, {"img": "", "name": "Polycab"}, {"img": "", "name": "Panasonic"}, {"img": "", "name": "boAt"}, {"img": "", "name": "Godrej"}, {"img": "", "name": "L&T"}, {"img": "", "name": "Blue Star"}, {"img": "", "name": "Prestige"}, {"img": "", "name": "Yash Fans"}], "phone": "9324622693", "risks": [{"risk": "Tooling vendor capacity delays during festival/year-end periods", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Pre-aligned vendor pool with 3 alternates; tooling slot booked at design-freeze stage, not at handover.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Component obsolescence in embedded BOM (semiconductors)", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Phase 3 BOM uses parts with minimum 5-year lifecycle commitment from manufacturers; second-source identified for >80% of critical components.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Regulatory certification timeline (BIS / EMC / FCC)", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Compliance touchpoints embedded in design phase, not deferred to post-prototype. Test lab slots reserved at Phase 2 sign-off.", "probability": "Low"}, {"risk": "Late client-side feedback creating design freeze drift", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Stage-gate calendar fixed in kick-off; delays beyond 7 working days trigger documented schedule renegotiation per Section 4 of T&C.", "probability": "High"}], "swift": "BCMLINBB", "acname": "IUOVA", "branch": "Mulund (West)", "client": "Srahi", "result": "A production-cleared, manufacturing-ready product platform — engineered for seamless tooling, vendor alignment, and scalable commercialization.", "address": "Office No 504, 5th Floor,\nFilix Tower, Mulund West,\nMumbai – 400078, Maharashtra", "concern": "Salil Arora", "project": "NA", "v1_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bcyXyAHh-P_M8MzZYUycJGC6e3C-mMmy/view", "v2_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Ln5IMV4P5jMzIQtEIBnAWjuFt5JfF77/view", "outcomes": [{"body": "Curated design directions with refined CMF options and high-quality visualizations, supported by clear engineering rationale.", "title": "Industrial Design & CMF Package"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade 3D data optimized for tooling, scalability, and seamless production integration.", "title": "Tooling-Ready CAD Release"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade PCB and Gerber files. Optimized for scalability and seamless production integration.", "title": "Production Ready Electronics"}, {"body": "Precision-built prototype for real-world validation of form, fit, and performance.", "title": "Functional Prototype (As per scope)"}, {"body": "Comprehensive technical documentation validating manufacturability, performance, and risk mitigation.", "title": "Engineering & Validation Reports (As per scope)"}], "packages": [{"id": "pkg_gqd8u9w", "label": "Foundation Package", "phases": [{"inr": 396000, "name": "Phase 1 - Industrial Design + CMF with Schematics", "weeks": "5", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Kick off meeting & brief discussion", "Brainstorming & Ideation on schematic", "Client review & refinement of schematic", "Brainstorming & Concept Ideation for design", "Internal review & refinement of Design", "Concept