plan\",\"target\":\"≥ 90% pass rate\"},{\"metric\":\"Final BOM cost variance vs. quoted target\",\"target\":\"≤ 5% deviation\"}]}","{\"id\":\"pkg_tczzaqs\",\"is_custom\":false,\"label\":\"Flagship Package\",\"enabled\":true,\"productName\":\"NA\",\"phases\":[{\"name\":\"Phase 1 - Industrial Design + CMF with Schematics\",\"weeks\":\"4\",\"inr\":594000,\"activities\":[\"Kick off meeting & brief discussion\",\"Brainstorming & Ideation on schematic\",\"Client review & refinement of schematic\",\"Brainstorming & Concept Ideation for design\",\"Internal review & refinement of Design\",\"Concept 3D models\",\"Concept Renders\",\"ID presentation\",\"Client review & ID Refinement\",\"Final Presentation\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) Design presentation with 4 concept designs.\\n2) 3 CMF combinations for selected concept.\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 1.1 – Alpha Prototype\",\"weeks\":\"Included\",\"inr\":\"Included\",\"activities\":[],\"deliverables\":\"Visual prototype of all 4 concepts with one selected CMF option.\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 2 - Product Engineering & Prototyping\",\"weeks\":\"6\",\"inr\":385000,\"activities\":[\"3D CAD models\",\"Review, update CAD files\",\"Engineering review & Updated CAD files\",\"File submission for prototyping/mold maker''s review\",\"Updated CAD files based on prototype/mold maker''s feedback\",\"Internal review & Engineering refinement\",\"Value Engineering\",\"Final submission\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) Engineering 3D CAD file of one selected concept''s components & Assembly based on final prototype. (Step or Parasolid)\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 2.1 - 2D CAD Drawings\",\"weeks\":\"Included\",\"inr\":\"Included\",\"activities\":[],\"deliverables\":\"1) 2D drawings of selected concept. (In IUOVA''s drawing format)\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 2.2 – Beta Prototype\",\"weeks\":\"-\",\"inr\":\"As per Actual\",\"activities\":[],\"deliverables\":\"1) Functional/Near real Prototype as per approved materials.\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 3 - Electrical & Electronics Development\",\"weeks\":\"12\",\"inr\":850000,\"activities\":[\"Identify the components\",\"PCB architecture\",\"PCB design\",\"Review & refinements\",\"Final PCB design submission\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) Embedded Hardware (Bill Of Materials)\\n2) Embedded Software (Gerber File)\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 3.1 – PCB Prototype\",\"weeks\":\"Included\",\"inr\":\"Included\",\"activities\":[],\"deliverables\":\"1) One Prototype of PCB for POC.\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 4 - Product Validation\",\"weeks\":\"3\",\"inr\":200000,\"activities\":[\"Load test/stress analysis\",\"Drop test\",\"Thermal analysis\",\"FEA simulation\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) One report of CFD Analysis (2 Iterations).\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 5 – Manufacturing Readiness, Vendor Development & Sourcing\",\"weeks\":\"3\",\"inr\":200000,\"activities\":[\"Vendor development\",\"Tool development\",\"Batch production\",\"Component Sourcing\"],\"deliverables\":\"-\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Additional Phase 6 - Product Strategy, 360 Research Architecture\",\"weeks\":\"-\",\"inr\":\"-\",\"activities\":[\"Online & Offline survey\",\"Client study\",\"E-commerce study\",\"Area of opportunities as per survey\",\"Geographic study\",\"CMF study\",\"Threshold\"],\"deliverables\":\"-\",\"enabled\":true},{\"name\":\"Phase 7 - Packaging Development\",\"weeks\":\"2\",\"inr\":120000,\"activities\":[\"Packaging design development \",\"Product placement and protection approach\",\"Packaging graphics & product communication\",\"Material & finish selection\",\"Packaging refinement & finalisation\"],\"deliverables\":\"1) Final packaging design\\n2) 3D packaging visualisation using existing product CAD\\n3) Packaging specification sheet (material, finish & dimensions)\\n4) Final vendor handover files\",\"enabled\":true}],\"paymentSummary\":[\"50% Advance, 30% against Phase 1 and 20% against Project handover.\",\"Cost of all Prototyping is extra as per applicable.\",\"Quote is inclusive of all taxes.\",\"Any additions or changes to the Scope of Work (SOW) after finalizing the design or beyond three iterations will incur additional charges as applicable.\"],\"timeline\":\"29-30 Weeks from Commencement of Project.\",\"deliverablesNote\":\"As per above mentioned.\",\"bankDetailsNote\":\"See \\\"Project Investment & Banking\\\" page for full wire transfer details.\",\"outOfScope\":[\"Mass production tooling, mold making, and tool fabrication costs\",\"Regulatory certifications (BIS, EMC, FCC, CE) — quoted separately\",\"IP filings, design registration government fees, and trademark prosecution\",\"Post-launch warranty support beyond 30 days from handover\"],\"successMetrics\":[{\"metric\":\"Design freeze achieved within Phase 1 timeline\",\"target\":\"4 weeks from kick-off\"},{\"metric\":\"CAD files reviewed and signed off by tooling partner\",\"target\":\"≥ 1 vendor sign-off\"},{\"metric\":\"Prototype passes agreed-upon test plan\",\"target\":\"≥ 90% pass rate\"},{\"metric\":\"Final BOM cost variance vs. quoted target\",\"target\":\"≤ 5% deviation\"}]}"}', 0, 'Draft', '{"fx": 90, "tc": [{"items": ["The Client shall provide complete and detailed information before project commencement to ensure accurate delivery."], "title": "Project Initiation"}, {"items": ["Client must make payments as per payment schedule in agreement, delay in payments more that 30 days will incur additional delay charges of 5% of total fees and work will be halted. It will commence once payments are cleared.", "Invoicing need to complete within 7 days of milestone completion.", "Travelling will be billed as per actual for onsite client or vendor visits."], "title": "Payment Terms"}, {"items": ["We will provide fair concepts based on client inputs and feedback.", "Clients are allowed up to three revisions; additional revisions will incur extra charges as mutually agreed.", "Modifications after finalizing the design and CAD files will be treated as additional scope of work and will incur additional charges as mutually agreed."], "title": "Concept Development and Revisions"}, {"items": ["Client-induced delays exceeding 2 months will incur waiting charges of 10% of the total fees per delayed week.", "Client must make complete payment once the services are delivered by IUOVA, till that ownership of the developed Design/Product associated with the project remains with IUOVA."], "title": "Delays and Waiting Charges"}, {"items": ["Work outside the original scope of work will be charged based on the quantum of work or a mutually agreed value."], "title": "Additional Work"}, {"items": ["Mutual consent is required for project cancellation.", "Client-initiated cancellations: advance payments are non-refundable.", "IUOVA-initiated cancellations (due to client fault): client must clear payments for work done."], "title": "Project Cancellation"}, {"items": ["Any information that is publicly available will not be treated as confidential or covered under IP, patent, or NDA terms.", "No alterations or changes to the work without IUOVA''s consent during the project timeframe and validity period.", "Post-completion modifications will incur additional fees.", "IUOVA Design Company will transfer the Design Registration to the client for the selected concepts only."], "title": "Intellectual Property and Modifications"}, {"items": ["Iuova would like to publish some case study of the project for our brand development initiative.", "With approval from client would publish on its website and social media platforms.", "IUOVA would also do some video testimonials with client for the same."], "title": "Promotion and Portfolio"}, {"items": ["Bugs Fix type support will be provided from IUOVA for the deliverables associated with the project only for 30 days post handover."], "title": "Warranty"}], "gst": 18, "rfq": {"id": "108050c6-817a-4ad8-9f1a-498ed3132228", "budget": "10 -15 Lakhs INR (Upto 20000 USD)", "services": ["Product Design Services (Industrial Design), Product Engineering Services., Prototyping Services, Manufacturing Services"], "timeline": "3 -4 months", "company_info": "We are Startup, Founded by 4 friends, having Engineering background from IIT. We are preparing ourself to enter in to Home Appliance smart solution segment. First, We have decided to enter in to Air Purifier market.", "business_size": "0 -10 Crores INR", "hear_about_us": "Google", "project_scope": "PARK Innovations seeks a qualified engineering design partner to develop the PAR-400, a residential air purifier targeting the Indian and outside market. The objective is to deliver 5 functional EVT (Engineering Verification Test) units suitable for investor demonstrations, regulatory pre-compliance testing, and field trials.\nThis is not a conceptual industrial design exercise. We require a manufacturing-ready engineering package that proves the product can be mass-produced within strict cost targets (BOM ₹5,500–7,500 at 5k volume) while meeting performance benchmarks (CADR 300 m³/h, Noise <51 dB(A)).\nYour Scope: Complete mechanical, electrical, and firmware engineering; soft-tooling for representative parts; assembly of 2 working prototypes; validation testing documentation.", "has_components": true, "form_experience": 5, "has_manufacturing": false, "manufacturing_moq": "5000", "additional_details": "REQUEST FOR PROPOSAL (RFP) – ENGINEERING DESIGN & PROTOTYPE DEVELOPMENT\nTO: Design & Engineering Consultancies / Product Development Firms\nFROM: PARK Innovations Pvt. Ltd.\nPROJECT: PAR-400 Residential Air Purifier – Concept to Investment-Ready Prototype\nDATE: January 30, 2026\n\n1. EXECUTIVE SUMMARY\nPARK Innovations seeks a qualified engineering design partner to develop the PAR-400, a residential air purifier targeting the Indian and outside market. The objective is to deliver 5 functional EVT (Engineering Verification Test) units suitable for investor demonstrations, regulatory pre-compliance testing, and field trials.\nThis is not a conceptual industrial design exercise. We require a manufacturing-ready engineering package that proves the product can be mass-produced within strict cost targets (BOM ₹5,500–7,500 at 5k volume) while meeting performance benchmarks (CADR 300 m³/h, Noise <51 dB(A)).\nYour Scope: Complete mechanical, electrical, and firmware engineering; soft-tooling for representative parts; assembly of 2 working prototypes; validation testing documentation.\n\n2. SCOPE OF WORK (PHASED DELIVERABLES)\n\nPhase 1: Engineering Design & Analysis\nObjective: Frozen CAD and engineering documentation ready for prototyping.\nDeliverables Required:\nIndustrial Design Refinement: Finalize CMF (Color-Material-Finish) for investor presentation; ergonomics validation for Indian households (floor/desktop dual use).\nMechanical Engineering:\nComplete 3D CAD (SolidWorks/CREO, native files + STEP), fully manufacturable using injection molding and sheet metal.\n2D manufacturing drawings (GD&T per ISO 1101) for all custom parts.\nTolerance stack-up analysis (critical: filter sealing, fan balance, PCB fit).\nStructural FEA: Drop test simulation (ISTA 2A standard), vibration analysis for shipping.\nElectrical Engineering:\nSchematic capture (Altium/OrCAD) and PCB Layout (2-layer, SMT,single-sided load).\nBOM selection for all electronic components\nFirmware architecture: Sensor fusion (PM2.5 + optional TVOC), motor PID control, touch HMI, error handling.\nAirflow Engineering: CFD analysis of fan volute and filter housing; pressure drop verification; acoustic simulation (frequency response prediction).\n\nPhase 2: Design for Manufacturing (DFM) & Soft Tooling \nObjective: Bridge tooling for prototype parts that represent final production quality.\nDeliverables Required:\nDFM Reports: Mold flow analysis for ABS housings; draft angle verification; sink mark prediction.\nSoft Tooling Production:\nAluminum/Silicone bridge molds for housing components (2 sets: upper/lower).\nForming tools for sheet metal grille components.\nLow-volume injection molding of 10 sets of parts (allowing for 2 assemblies + spares).\nFirst Article Inspection (FAI): Dimension reports for molded parts against 2D drawings.\n\nPhase 3: EVT Prototype Assembly\nObjective: 2 fully functional, investor-presentable units.\nDeliverables Required:\nPCB Assembly: Populated and tested circuit boards (ICT/Boundary scan).\nMechanical Integration: Full assembly of 2 units using soft-tooled parts and off-the-shelf components (fans, sensors).\nCalibration: PM2.5 sensor calibration against reference instrument; fan curve mapping; noise measurement.\nTest Reports:\nPerformance: CADR testing per ANSI/AHAM AC-1 protocol (smoke/turbidity method).\nSafety: Dielectric strength, leakage current, temperature rise (pre-compliance to IS 13252).\nReliability: 500-hour continuous run test on 2 units.\n\nPhase 4: Design Validation & Documentation (Weeks 14-16)\nObjective: Package suitable for investor due diligence and factory handover.\nDeliverables Required:\nDesign History File (DHF): Complete engineering change log, calculation notebooks, test data.\nManufacturing Transfer Package: Production-ready drawings, suggested supplier list (SSPL), assembly instructions (SOPs).\nInvestor Presentation Support: High-quality renderings, exploded views, cost analysis validation, competitive benchmarking report.\n\n3. TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS (MANDATORY REQUIREMENTS)\n3.1 Performance Targets\n\nTest Method: CADR (Smoke) ≥280 m³/h ANSI/AHAM AC-1\nCoverage Area: 350–400 sq ft @ 4.8 ACH\nCalculated from CADR\nNoise Level\n≤55 dB(A) @ Turbo (1m); ≤32 dB(A) @ Sleep\nIEC 60704-2-1\nPower Consumption\n≤40W (Turbo); ≤5W (Sleep)\nPower meter\nFilter Life\n6 months (HEPA); 12 months (Carbon)\nCalculated based on usage model\n\n3.2 Cost Constraints (Critical)\nTarget BOM Cost: INR 5,500–7,000 per unit at 10,000 MOQ (current pricing).\nDesign to Cost: All component selections must have identified suppliers with quoted pricing; no \"gold plating\" or over-specification.\nManufacturing Processes: Restricted to high-volume capable methods:\nInjection molding (thermoplastics: ABS, PC/ABS, PA6-GF)\nSheet metal stamping (galvanized steel, aluminum)\nPCB SMT/THT\nUltrasonic welding (filter sealing)\n\n3.3 Regulatory & Safety\nPrimary: IS 13252 (Information Technology Equipment Safety - harmonized with IEC 60950/62368)\nEMC: CISPR 32 Class B (residential) pre-compliance\nRoHS: All materials must be RoHS 3 compliant for future export capability\n\n3.4 Design Specifics\nForm Factor: Vertical tower, max height 650mm, footprint ≤250×250mm\nAirflow: Bottom 360° intake → Pre-filter → HEPA H13 → Activated Carbon → Top discharge\nControls: Capacitive touch (3 speeds + Auto), PM2.5 LED indicator ring (traffic light colors), Filter reset button\nPower: 220-240V AC, 50Hz, internal SMPS (universal input 100-240V preferred if cost-neutral)\n\n4. DELIVERABLES CHECKLIST FOR FINAL HANDOVER\nYour firm must provide the following at project completion:\nEngineering Data\n[ ] Native CAD files (SolidWorks 2022 or CREO 8.0 compatible)\n[ ] Complete 2D drawing package (PDF + DWG) with GD&T\n[ ] PCB design files (Gerbers, drill files, pick-and-place files)\n[ ] Firmware source code (commented, with build instructions)\n[ ] Bill of Materials (BOM): Master BOM and EBOM (Engineering BOM) with manufacturer part numbers and supplier contacts\nPrototypes\n[ ] 2× fully functional EVT units ( aesthetically finished, \"investor-ready\" appearance)\n[ ] 1× \"engineering mule\" (transparent/translucent housing for airflow visualization, if possible)\n[ ] Spare components kit (1 extra fan assemblies, 2 extra PCBs, 2 extra filter sets)\nDocumentation\n[ ] DFMEA (Design Failure Mode Effects Analysis)\n[ ] Test Reports: CADR validation, Noise measurement, Safety pre-compliance, Thermal imaging\n[ ] Assembly Instructions: Illustrated SOPs suitable for semi-skilled Indian labor\n[ ] Service Manual: Troubleshooting guide, filter replacement procedure, calibration protocol\n[ ] Cost Analysis Report: Validated BOM costing with 3 quotes per critical component (fan, sensor, filters)\nIP & Legal\n[ ] Invention Disclosure: List of any patentable innovations discovered during development (ownership: PARK Innovations)\n[ ] Design Rights: Assignment of all industrial design rights to PARK Innovations\n[ ] Third-Party IP Clearance: Confirmation that no open-source contamination (GPL/copyleft) exists in firmware without disclosure\n\n5. PROJECT TIMELINE\nApproximate Duration: 16 weeks from kickoff to final delivery\nKey Milestones:\nWeek 2: Design Review 1 (Architecture frozen)\nWeek 4: Critical Design Review (CDR) – CAD complete, PCB layout released\nWeek 9: First Parts Ready (FAI acceptable)\nWeek 12: Alpha Build (power-on, basic function)\nWeek 14: Beta Build (5 units complete, testing started)\nWeek 16: Final Delivery (documentation + prototypes)\n\n\n6. INVESTOR-READINESS REQUIREMENTS\nSince these prototypes will be used for Series A fundraising, specific attention must be paid to:\nAesthetic Quality: Soft-tooled parts must achieve 90% of final production surface finish (no visible layer lines, proper texture)\nDemo Reliability: Units must survive 20+ demonstrations without failure (robust cable management, strain relief)\nData Package: Prepare a \"Technical Investment Memorandum\" summarizing:\nCompetitive teardown analysis (vs. Xiaomi, Honeywell, Dyson)\nManufacturing margin analysis (COGS vs. retail price)\nScalability assessment (supplier capacity, tooling investment required for 100k units)\nPatent Support: Provide technical descriptions and sketches for any novel features (sealing mechanisms, airflow paths) to support provisional patent filings.\n\n7. COMMERCIAL TERMS & EVALUATION CRITERIA\nBudget Expectation\nBudget Range: ₹18,00,000 – ₹25,00,000 (all-inclusive: engineering, soft tooling, 5 prototypes, testing)\nPayment Terms: 30% kickoff, 30% CDR, 20% First Build, 20% Final Delivery\nCurrency: INR; Taxes as applicable (GST)\nEvaluation Criteria (Weightage)\nTechnical Capability (40%): Demonstrated experience in HVAC, consumer appliances, or mechatronic products\nSpeed to Market (25%): Realistic schedule with buffer management\nCost Engineering (20%): Evidence of prior DTC (Design to Cost) success in consumer electronics\nGeographic Presence (15%): Preference for firms with presence in India (Delhi NCR, Bangalore, or Mumbai) for ease of collaboration; however, global firms with Indian partners accepted\nSubmission Requirements\nPlease submit your proposal including:\nTechnical Approach: Methodology for Phase 1-4, team structure, software tools\nPortfolio: Relevant case studies (2-3 consumer appliances or similar complexity)\nDetailed Cost Breakdown: Engineering hours, tooling costs, prototype materials, project management\nRisk Register: Your assessment of top 3 technical risks and mitigation strategies\nReferences: 2 client references for similar prototype development projects\n\n8. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY & CONFIDENTIALITY\nAll information shared by PARK Innovations is under NDA.\nAll inventions, designs, and code developed under this project shall be the exclusive property of PARK Innovations.\nYour firm may retain copies for internal portfolio purposes only with written permission (anonymized until product launch).\n\n", "components_details": "We will be developing Mobile based App and Firmware", "important_features": "Product Type : High-Efficiency Room Air Purifier\nFeatures : Basic\nColour: Mat Gray / Mat White\nPrimary Material: High-Impact ABS Plastic\nSecondary Material: \n-\nInternet connectivity: Wi-Fi (2.4 GHz) + Bluetooth (for easy pairing)\nAutomatic speed Mode: Yes\nSleep Mode: Yes\nAir purifying speeds setting: Manual (5-8 Speeds)\nChild Lock: Yes\n-\nTimer: 2h / 4h / 8h settings via App/Touch\nAir Quality feedback: PM2.5 Value \n3-Color LED Ring (Green/Orange/Red) for AQI\n\n\nTechnical Specifications\n\nPower input (Voltage) - 220-240V AC (Device Input: 24V DC)\nRated Power- 40W (Max)\nAmount of Perticulate Clean Air (CADR) - 280 - 320 m3/hr\n\nUV LED: Yes\nApplicable Area - Up to 350-400 sq. ft.\nNoise (High Speed)- 52 dB\nNoise (Low Speed)- 30 dB\nFilter Layers: 3 Layers (Fabric Pre-filter, H13 HEPA, Active Carbon)\nRecommended Filter Change: Yes\nAir Quality Sensors: PM2.5", "require_manufacturing": true}, "web": "www.iuovadesign.com", "acno": "005212100004508", "bank": "Bharat Co-Operative Bank Ltd.", "date": "30-01-2026", "faqs": [{"a": "A freelancer typically delivers one slice (just ID, or just CAD). A low-cost agency may deliver more slices but rarely with end-to-end accountability. IUOVA brings industrial design, engineering, electronics, prototyping, and manufacturing readiness under one roof, with a senior team that has shipped 200+ products to market. The cost difference reflects the difference between getting a design and getting a market-ready product platform — engineered for tooling, validated through prototyping, and supplier-aligned for manufacturing.", "q": "Why work with IUOVA over a freelancer or a cheaper agency?"}, {"a": "Our core team is 15–30 designers, engineers, and project managers across industrial design, mechanical engineering, electronics, and operations. For each engagement, we lock a named project team at kick-off — typically 4–6 people scaled to project complexity. We deliberately maintain a buffer of 20–25% spare capacity across the studio so urgent client requests don''t cascade into delays. Concurrent project load per senior team member is capped at 2–3 active engagements to ensure depth of attention. Timeline commitments are made only after capacity confirmation in kick-off.", "q": "What is your team size and how do you ensure capacity to deliver on time?"}, {"a": "Yes. While our Foundation/Growth/Flagship packages are designed as integrated workflows, individual phases can be engaged à la carte. Common à la carte engagements: ID-only sprint (2–3 weeks), engineering-only for clients with frozen ID (3–4 weeks), PCB development for mechanical-complete products (8–10 weeks). The proposal will quote your specific scope, and we will flag any handoff dependencies (e.g., engineering needs CAD-ready ID input). Pricing is published in our Custom Package templates.", "q": "Can we buy just industrial design, just engineering, or just electronics — without the full package?"}, {"a": "Industrial design: Adobe Creative Suite, Vizcom (AI rendering), KeyShot for visualization. Mechanical CAD: SolidWorks (primary), Fusion 360, NX for complex assemblies. Drawings: AutoCAD. Simulation: Ansys for FEA, basic CFD; SolidWorks Simulation for stress/thermal. Electronics: Altium Designer (primary PCB), KiCad for open-source projects, EasyEDA for rapid prototyping. Firmware: PlatformIO, ESP-IDF, STM32CubeIDE. Project management: Notion, Slack, Loom for async reviews. We deliver source files in industry-standard formats so the client is never locked to our specific tool stack.", "q": "What software and tools do you use for design and engineering?"}, {"a": "If cancellation happens within 7 days of signing AND before the kick-off meeting, we refund the 50% advance minus a 10% engagement fee that covers team reservation, contracting, and admin overhead. After kick-off has occurred, the engagement is considered live and standard milestone-based payment terms apply (the advance is non-refundable, but no further payments are due if the project is cancelled). Written cancellation notice is required in either case.", "q": "What if we sign the proposal but need to cancel before kick-off?"}, {"a": "Every phase has a defined Definition of Done documented in the proposal scope. At phase end, we hold a structured review where the client either signs off or flags issues. Any flagged issues are resolved within the included revision budget (3 rounds per phase). Sign-off is recorded via email confirmation or a signed phase completion certificate, which triggers the next milestone payment. Without sign-off, the project does not progress to the next phase — protecting both parties from scope drift and disputed deliverables.", "q": "What is the acceptance criteria — how is each phase signed off?"}, {"a": "Our development framework is specifically designed to mitigate this risk through a structured, stage-gated process. We incorporate client validation checkpoints at each critical phase—ideation, sketch development, and concept presentation—ensuring alignment on design direction before progressing further. In the event that the proposed concepts do not meet expectations, we initiate a controlled second iteration cycle within the ideation phase. This allows us to recalibrate design direction based on structured feedback while maintaining overall project timelines. Such scenarios are rare due to our continuous validation approach, but the process is built to accommodate them as a defined fallback.", "q": "What if we don''t like the design concepts presented?"}, {"a": "Our public portfolio at iuovadesign.com is organized by category — consumer electronics, smart appliances, industrial products, wearables, and IoT devices. We have shipped products with Bajaj, Havells, Crompton, Siemens, Polycab, Panasonic, boAt, Godrej, L&T, Blue Star, and Prestige across these categories. For your specific category, we will share relevant case studies under NDA at the qualifying call. If we have not done your exact product before, we will be transparent about it and explain what adjacent expertise applies.", "q": "Have you worked on products in our specific category before?"}, {"a": "For Indian clients, all invoices include 18% GST as per current regulations. Our GSTIN is provided on the formal invoice. TDS, where applicable on professional services, can be deducted by the client and the certificate sent to us — we will reconcile against the final invoice. International clients receive a USD-denominated invoice with no GST, suitable for foreign exchange payment via SWIFT. Invoices are issued at the start of each milestone (advance, Phase 1 sign-off, handover) and are payable within 7 working days.", "q": "How is GST treated, and what is your invoice format?"}, {"a": "For 30 days post-handover, we provide free corrective work for any defect directly traceable to our deliverables — design errors, drawing mistakes, missing specifications, etc. Beyond this period, our maximum liability is capped at the total fees paid for the engagement, in line with standard product design industry contracts. We carry professional indemnity insurance covering the work product. We do not bear liability for third-party manufacturing defects, vendor errors, end-user misuse, or downstream product market performance.", "q": "What is your warranty and liability cap on delivered designs?"}, {"a": "Yes — many of our engagements are confidential by design, particularly for startup clients in stealth mode or established brands launching disruptive products. We sign mutual NDAs before any technical details are shared, restrict project access to a named core team, segment file storage from the rest of our infrastructure, and contractually exclude the project from our public portfolio (or include it only after public launch with permission). For exceptional secrecy needs, we can offer code-named project tracking and escrow-based deliverable handover.", "q": "Can you work under deep secrecy on stealth-mode products?"}], "ifsc": "BCBM0000053", "logo": "/assets/holder_logo-CW7spHUh.png", "refs": "Crompton\nPolycab\nYash Fans\nBajaj Electricals\nNational Plastics\nDover Brookes\nHelpmesee\nMyro\nPrestige\nPreethi\nBoat", "about": "Iuova Design Company is an Award-winning Product Innovation Partner, providing end to end Product Development Solutions.\n\nOver the years, We have developed more than 200 Products in categories such as – Home & Kitchen Appliances, Consumer Electronics, Medical Devices, Home Automation, Metal Enclosures and many more.", "email": "info@iuova.in", "logos": [{"img": "", "name": "Bajaj Electricals"}, {"img": "", "name": "Havells"}, {"img": "", "name": "Crompton"}, {"img": "", "name": "Siemens"}, {"img": "", "name": "Polycab"}, {"img": "", "name": "Panasonic"}, {"img": "", "name": "boAt"}, {"img": "", "name": "Godrej"}, {"img": "", "name": "L&T"}, {"img": "", "name": "Blue Star"}, {"img": "", "name": "Prestige"}, {"img": "", "name": "Yash Fans"}], "phone": "8828586370", "risks": [{"risk": "Tooling vendor capacity delays during festival/year-end periods", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Pre-aligned vendor pool with 3 alternates; tooling slot booked at design-freeze stage, not at handover.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Component obsolescence in embedded BOM (semiconductors)", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Phase 3 BOM uses parts with minimum 5-year lifecycle commitment from manufacturers; second-source identified for >80% of critical components.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Regulatory certification timeline (BIS / EMC / FCC)", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Compliance touchpoints embedded in design phase, not deferred to post-prototype. Test lab slots reserved at Phase 2 sign-off.", "probability": "Low"}, {"risk": "Late client-side feedback creating design freeze drift", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Stage-gate calendar fixed in kick-off; delays beyond 7 working days trigger documented schedule renegotiation per Section 4 of T&C.", "probability": "High"}], "swift": "BCMLINBB", "acname": "IUOVA", "branch": "Mulund (West)", "client": "Park Innovations", "result": "A production-cleared, manufacturing-ready product platform — engineered for seamless tooling, vendor alignment, and scalable commercialization.", "address": "Office No 504, 5th Floor,\nFilix Tower, Mulund West,\nMumbai – 400078, Maharashtra", "concern": "Alok Niranjan", "project": "NA", "v1_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bcyXyAHh-P_M8MzZYUycJGC6e3C-mMmy/view", "v2_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Ln5IMV4P5jMzIQtEIBnAWjuFt5JfF77/view", "outcomes": [{"body": "Curated design directions with refined CMF options and high-quality visualizations, supported by clear engineering rationale.", "title": "Industrial Design & CMF Package"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade 3D data optimized for tooling, scalability, and seamless production integration.", "title": "Tooling-Ready CAD Release"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade PCB and Gerber files. Optimized for scalability and seamless production integration.", "title": "Production Ready Electronics"}, {"body": "Precision-built prototype for real-world validation of form, fit, and performance.", "title": "Functional Prototype (As per scope)"}, {"body": "Comprehensive technical documentation validating manufacturability, performance, and risk mitigation.", "title": "Engineering & Validation Reports (As per scope)"}], "packages": [{"id": "pkg_kz37y0b", "label": "Foundation Package", "phases": [{"inr": 396000, "name": "Phase 1 - Industrial Design + CMF with Schematics", "weeks": "5", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Kick off meeting & brief discussion", "Brainstorming & Ideation on schematic", "Client review & refinement of schematic", "Brainstorming & Concept Ideation for design", "Internal review & refinement of Design", "Concept 3D models", "Concept Renders", "ID presentation", "Client review & ID Refinement", "Final Presentation"], "deliverables": "1) Design presentation with 2 concept designs.\n2) 3 CMF combinations for selected concept."}, {"inr": "As per actual", "name": "Phase 1.1 – Alpha Prototype", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "1) One Visual prototype of selected concept."}, {"inr": 299000, "name": "Phase 2 - Product Engineering & Prototyping", "weeks": "5", "enabled": true, "activities": ["3D CAD models", "Review, update CAD files", "Engineering review & Updated CAD files", "File submission for prototyping/mold mak