s."}', '2026-09-22 20:44:21.236+00', '2026-09-22 20:44:21.236+00', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL),
	('tc_44hnat03f', 'Force24 Lifestyle Private Limited', 'Extension Board Development', 'Sharif Khan', 'force24sa@gmail.com', '9545670880', '{NULL,NULL,NULL}', 3026000, 'Sent', '{"fx": 90, "tc": [{"items": ["The Client shall provide complete and detailed information before project commencement to ensure accurate delivery."], "title": "Project Initiation"}, {"items": ["Client must make payments as per payment schedule in agreement, delay in payments more that 30 days will incur additional delay charges of 5% of total fees and work will be halted. It will commence once payments are cleared.", "Invoicing need to complete within 7 days of milestone completion.", "Travelling will be billed as per actual for onsite client or vendor visits."], "title": "Payment Terms"}, {"items": ["We will provide fair concepts based on client inputs and feedback.", "Clients are allowed up to three revisions; additional revisions will incur extra charges as mutually agreed.", "Modifications after finalizing the design and CAD files will be treated as additional scope of work and will incur additional charges as mutually agreed."], "title": "Concept Development and Revisions"}, {"items": ["Client-induced delays exceeding 2 months will incur waiting charges of 10% of the total fees per delayed week.", "Client must make complete payment once the services are delivered by IUOVA, till that ownership of the developed Design/Product associated with the project remains with IUOVA."], "title": "Delays and Waiting Charges"}, {"items": ["Work outside the original scope of work will be charged based on the quantum of work or a mutually agreed value."], "title": "Additional Work"}, {"items": ["Mutual consent is required for project cancellation.", "Client-initiated cancellations: advance payments are non-refundable.", "IUOVA-initiated cancellations (due to client fault): client must clear payments for work done."], "title": "Project Cancellation"}, {"items": ["Any information that is publicly available will not be treated as confidential or covered under IP, patent, or NDA terms.", "No alterations or changes to the work without IUOVA''s consent during the project timeframe and validity period.", "Post-completion modifications will incur additional fees.", "IUOVA Design Company will transfer the Design Registration to the client for the selected concepts only."], "title": "Intellectual Property and Modifications"}, {"items": ["Iuova would like to publish some case study of the project for our brand development initiative.", "With approval from client would publish on its website and social media platforms.", "IUOVA would also do some video testimonials with client for the same."], "title": "Promotion and Portfolio"}, {"items": ["Bugs Fix type support will be provided from IUOVA for the deliverables associated with the project only for 30 days post handover."], "title": "Warranty"}], "gst": 18, "rfq": {"id": "7ec356aa-4f4c-4428-a465-c3981a17f980", "budget": "5 - 10 Lakhs INR (Upto 10000 USD)", "services": ["Product Design Services (Industrial Design)", "Product Engineering Services", "Prototyping Services", "Product Analysis Services", "Manufacturing Services"], "timeline": "0 - 1 months", "company_info": "Force24 Lifestyle Pvt. Ltd. is an Indian consumer products company engaged in the development, sourcing and marketing of practical lifestyle, home and electrical products. We sell products through major e-commerce channels and are currently expanding our product portfolio into consumer electrical products, including extension boards and related power accessories.\n\nFor this project, we are looking for an experienced product development and manufacturing partner who can support us from product engineering and prototyping through compliance and mass production.", "business_size": "0 - 10 Crores INR", "hear_about_us": "Google", "project_scope": "Development of a premium 5-socket extension board/power strip for the Indian market under our Force24 brand. The product concept, visual direction and key features have already been defined by us.\n\nScope required includes refinement of industrial design, complete mechanical and electrical engineering, component selection, safety design, DFM/DFA, 3D CAD development, functional prototyping, testing and preparation of production-ready drawings/BOM.\n\nThe product should be engineered for reliable mass production and compliance with applicable Indian safety/BIS requirements. We would also like support in identifying suitable manufacturing processes, tooling requirements and production partners where required.", "has_components": false, "form_experience": 5, "has_manufacturing": false, "manufacturing_moq": "1000", "additional_details": "Product Category: Electrical and electronic products\nOrganization Type: Retailer or e-commerce brand\n\nWe would like to understand your end-to-end capabilities for this project, particularly:\n\n• Whether electrical/electronic engineering and safety compliance are handled in-house\n• Experience developing extension boards, power strips or similar mains-powered electrical products\n• Support available for BIS certification/testing and applicable Indian standards\n• Prototype development process, expected iterations and prototype costs\n• Injection mould/tooling development capabilities and estimated tooling approach\n• Whether you can support component sourcing and vendor development in India\n• Whether manufacturing can be arranged directly through your facility or approved manufacturing partners\n• Ownership of final CAD files, drawings, BOM, tooling and other intellectual property after project completion\n• Estimated development timeline from concept refinement to production-ready prototype\n• Indicative NRE/development, prototyping and tooling costs\n• MOQ and indicative production cost at different volume levels, if manufacturing support is provided\n\nWe already have a defined product concept and visual direction and can share our reference renders after initial discussion. We are looking for a partner who can convert the concept into a safe, compliant and commercially manufacturable product while maintaining the intended Force24 design identity.", "components_details": "", "important_features": "• 5 universal sockets suitable for Indian and commonly used international plugs\n• Red child-safety shutters integrated into each socket\n• Single master ON/OFF switch with integrated LED indication\n• Overload and surge protection\n• Appropriate earthing and electrical safety architecture\n• Fire-retardant, high-quality enclosure materials\n• Premium warm off-white textured front surface\n• Translucent crimson-red lower housing with a subtle frosted/rain-glass effect that partially obscures internal components\n• Smooth premium rounded corners and approximately 8° inclined ergonomic design\n• Anti-slip rubber feet and stable desktop construction\n• Approx. 2-5metre heavy-duty power cable with Indian 3-pin plug\n• Target rating around 10A / 250V AC, subject to engineering validation\n• Product must be designed for applicable Indian safety/BIS compliance and mass manufacturing\n• Design should allow efficient injection moulding, assembly, servicing and quality control", "require_manufacturing": false}, "web": "www.iuovadesign.com", "acno": "005212100004508", "bank": "Bharat Co-Operative Bank Ltd.", "date": "24-09-2026", "faqs": [{"a": "A freelancer typically delivers one slice (just ID, or just CAD). A low-cost agency may deliver more slices but rarely with end-to-end accountability. IUOVA brings industrial design, engineering, electronics, prototyping, and manufacturing readiness under one roof, with a senior team that has shipped 200+ products to market. The cost difference reflects the difference between getting a design and getting a market-ready product platform — engineered for tooling, validated through prototyping, and supplier-aligned for manufacturing.", "q": "Why work with IUOVA over a freelancer or a cheaper agency?"}, {"a": "Our core team is 15–30 designers, engineers, and project managers across industrial design, mechanical engineering, electronics, and operations. For each engagement, we lock a named project team at kick-off — typically 4–6 people scaled to project complexity. We deliberately maintain a buffer of 20–25% spare capacity across the studio so urgent client requests don''t cascade into delays. Concurrent project load per senior team member is capped at 2–3 active engagements to ensure depth of attention. Timeline commitments are made only after capacity confirmation in kick-off.", "q": "What is your team size and how do you ensure capacity to deliver on time?"}, {"a": "Yes. While our Foundation/Growth/Flagship packages are designed as integrated workflows, individual phases can be engaged à la carte. Common à la carte engagements: ID-only sprint (2–3 weeks), engineering-only for clients with frozen ID (3–4 weeks), PCB development for mechanical-complete products (8–10 weeks). The proposal will quote your specific scope, and we will flag any handoff dependencies (e.g., engineering needs CAD-ready ID input). Pricing is published in our Custom Package templates.", "q": "Can we buy just industrial design, just engineering, or just electronics — without the full package?"}, {"a": "Industrial design: Adobe Creative Suite, Vizcom (AI rendering), KeyShot for visualization. Mechanical CAD: SolidWorks (primary), Fusion 360, NX for complex assemblies. Drawings: AutoCAD. Simulation: Ansys for FEA, basic CFD; SolidWorks Simulation for stress/thermal. Electronics: Altium Designer (primary PCB), KiCad for open-source projects, EasyEDA for rapid prototyping. Firmware: PlatformIO, ESP-IDF, STM32CubeIDE. Project management: Notion, Slack, Loom for async reviews. We deliver source files in industry-standard formats so the client is never locked to our specific tool stack.", "q": "What software and tools do you use for design and engineering?"}, {"a": "If cancellation happens within 7 days of signing AND before the kick-off meeting, we refund the 50% advance minus a 10% engagement fee that covers team reservation, contracting, and admin overhead. After kick-off has occurred, the engagement is considered live and standard milestone-based payment terms apply (the advance is non-refundable, but no further payments are due if the project is cancelled). Written cancellation notice is required in either case.", "q": "What if we sign the proposal but need to cancel before kick-off?"}, {"a": "Every phase has a defined Definition of Done documented in the proposal scope. At phase end, we hold a structured review where the client either signs off or flags issues. Any flagged issues are resolved within the included revision budget (3 rounds per phase). Sign-off is recorded via email confirmation or a signed phase completion certificate, which triggers the next milestone payment. Without sign-off, the project does not progress to the next phase — protecting both parties from scope drift and disputed deliverables.", "q": "What is the acceptance criteria — how is each phase signed off?"}, {"a": "Our development framework is specifically designed to mitigate this risk through a structured, stage-gated process. We incorporate client validation checkpoints at each critical phase—ideation, sketch development, and concept presentation—ensuring alignment on design direction before progressing further. In the event that the proposed concepts do not meet expectations, we initiate a controlled second iteration cycle within the ideation phase. This allows us to recalibrate design direction based on structured feedback while maintaining overall project timelines. Such scenarios are rare due to our continuous validation approach, but the process is built to accommodate them as a defined fallback.", "q": "What if we don''t like the design concepts presented?"}, {"a": "Our public portfolio at iuovadesign.com is organized by category — consumer electronics, smart appliances, industrial products, wearables, and IoT devices. We have shipped products with Bajaj, Havells, Crompton, Siemens, Polycab, Panasonic, boAt, Godrej, L&T, Blue Star, and Prestige across these categories. For your specific category, we will share relevant case studies under NDA at the qualifying call. If we have not done your exact product before, we will be transparent about it and explain what adjacent expertise applies.", "q": "Have you worked on products in our specific category before?"}, {"a": "For Indian clients, all invoices include 18% GST as per current regulations. Our GSTIN is provided on the formal invoice. TDS, where applicable on professional services, can be deducted by the client and the certificate sent to us — we will reconcile against the final invoice. International clients receive a USD-denominated invoice with no GST, suitable for foreign exchange payment via SWIFT. Invoices are issued at the start of each milestone (advance, Phase 1 sign-off, handover) and are payable within 7 working days.", "q": "How is GST treated, and what is your invoice format?"}, {"a": "For 30 days post-handover, we provide free corrective work for any defect directly traceable to our deliverables — design errors, drawing mistakes, missing specifications, etc. Beyond this period, our maximum liability is capped at the total fees paid for the engagement, in line with standard product design industry contracts. We carry professional indemnity insurance covering the work product. We do not bear liability for third-party manufacturing defects, vendor errors, end-user misuse, or downstream product market performance.", "q": "What is your warranty and liability cap on delivered designs?"}, {"a": "Yes — many of our engagements are confidential by design, particularly for startup clients in stealth mode or established brands launching disruptive products. We sign mutual NDAs before any technical details are shared, restrict project access to a named core team, segment file storage from the rest of our infrastructure, and contractually exclude the project from our public portfolio (or include it only after public launch with permission). For exceptional secrecy needs, we can offer code-named project tracking and escrow-based deliverable handover.", "q": "Can you work under deep secrecy on stealth-mode products?"}, {"a": "Discounts for additional concepts apply only to the design phase, not the overall project. One extra concept beyond your primary selection is offered at 50% of the base concept fee. If you purchase a total of three concepts, the two additional concepts are charged at 40% of the base concept fee. All discounts apply only to the design phase cost.", "q": " What if we want to purchase more than one design concept?"}, {"a": "Yes — we can run multiple projects subject to project-team availability and scheduling. When you engage us on two concurrent projects, we include one complimentary secondary package (scope and delivery terms to be defined in the proposal). Final scheduling, resource allocation, and exact deliverables will be confirmed during scoping.", "q": "Can we run two projects with you at the same time?"}, {"a": "There are no additional design charges for creating size variants of a selected concept. Costs for size versions are limited to engineering, prototyping, testing, tooling (if applicable), and other development activities, which will be charged per our standard engineering and prototype pricing. Final costs are scoped and confirmed after an initial review to determine the required engineering effort for each size variant.", "q": "If we want the same selected design language but different size versions of the product, how is costing handled?"}], "ifsc": "BCBM0000053", "logo": "/assets/holder_logo-CW7spHUh.png", "refs": "Crompton\nPolycab\nYash Fans\nBajaj Electricals\nNational Plastics\nDover Brookes\nHelpmesee\nMyro\nPrestige\nPreethi\nBoat", "about": "Iuova Design Company is an Award-winning Product Innovation Partner, providing end to end Product Development Solutions.\n\nOver the years, We have developed more than 200 Products in categories such as – Home & Kitchen Appliances, Consumer Electronics, Medical Devices, Home Automation, Metal Enclosures and many more.", "email": "info@iuova.in", "logos": [{"img": "", "name": "Bajaj Electricals"}, {"img": "", "name": "Havells"}, {"img": "", "name": "Crompton"}, {"img": "", "name": "Siemens"}, {"img": "", "name": "Polycab"}, {"img": "", "name": "Panasonic"}, {"img": "", "name": "boAt"}, {"img": "", "name": "Godrej"}, {"img": "", "name": "L&T"}, {"img": "", "name": "Blue Star"}, {"img": "", "name": "Prestige"}, {"img": "", "name": "Yash Fans"}], "phone": "9545670880", "risks": [{"risk": "Tooling vendor capacity delays during festival/year-end periods", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Pre-aligned vendor pool with 3 alternates; tooling slot booked at design-freeze stage, not at handover.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Component obsolescence in embedded BOM (semiconductors)", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Phase 3 BOM uses parts with minimum 5-year lifecycle commitment from manufacturers; second-source identified for >80% of critical components.", "probability": "Medium"}, {"risk": "Regulatory certification timeline (BIS / EMC / FCC)", "impact": "High", "mitigation": "Compliance touchpoints embedded in design phase, not deferred to post-prototype. Test lab slots reserved at Phase 2 sign-off.", "probability": "Low"}, {"risk": "Late client-side feedback creating design freeze drift", "impact": "Medium", "mitigation": "Stage-gate calendar fixed in kick-off; delays beyond 7 working days trigger documented schedule renegotiation per Section 4 of T&C.", "probability": "High"}], "swift": "BCMLINBB", "acname": "IUOVA", "branch": "Mulund (West)", "client": "Force24 Lifestyle Private Limited", "result": "A production-cleared, manufacturing-ready product platform — engineered for seamless tooling, vendor alignment, and scalable commercialization.", "address": "Office No 504, 5th Floor,\nFilix Tower, Mulund West,\nMumbai – 400078, Maharashtra", "concern": "Sharif Khan", "project": "Extension Board Development", "v1_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1bcyXyAHh-P_M8MzZYUycJGC6e3C-mMmy/view", "v2_link": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18Ln5IMV4P5jMzIQtEIBnAWjuFt5JfF77/view", "outcomes": [{"body": "Curated design directions with refined CMF options and high-quality visualizations, supported by clear engineering rationale.", "title": "Industrial Design & CMF Package"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade 3D data optimized for tooling, scalability, and seamless production integration.", "title": "Tooling-Ready CAD Release"}, {"body": "Fully detailed, manufacturing-grade PCB and Gerber files. Optimized for scalability and seamless production integration.", "title": "Production Ready Electronics"}, {"body": "Precision-built prototype for real-world validation of form, fit, and performance.", "title": "Functional Prototype (As per scope)"}, {"body": "Comprehensive technical documentation validating manufacturability, performance, and risk mitigation.", "title": "Engineering & Validation Reports (As per scope)"}], "packages": [{"id": "pkg_oryg091", "note": "", "label": "Foundation Package", "phases": [{"inr": 396000, "name": "Phase 1 - Industrial Design + CMF with Schematics", "weeks": "4", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Kick off meeting & brief discussion", "Brainstorming & Ideation on schematic", "Client review & refinement of schematic", "Brainstorming & Concept Ideation for design", "Internal review & refinement of Design", "Concept 3D models", "Concept Renders", "ID presentation", "Client review & ID Refinement", "Final Presentation"], "deliverables": "1) Design presentation with 2 concept designs.\n2) 3 CMF combinations for selected concept."}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 1.1 – Alpha Prototype", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": 299000, "name": "Phase 2 - Product Engineering & Prototyping", "weeks": "4", "enabled": true, "activities": ["3D CAD models", "Review, update CAD files", "Engineering review & Updated CAD files", "File submission for prototyping/mold maker''s review", "Updated CAD files based on prototype/mold maker''s feedback", "Internal review & Engineering refinement", "Value Engineering", "Final submission"], "deliverables": "1) Engineering 3D CAD file of one selected concept''s components & Assembly based on final prototype. (Step or Parasolid)"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 2.1 - 2D CAD Drawings", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "As per Actuals", "name": "Phase 2.2 – Beta Prototype", "weeks": "As per Actuals", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "1) Functional/Near real Prototype as per approved materials."}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 3 - Electrical & Electronics Development", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Identify the components", "PCB architecture", "PCB design", "Review & refinements", "Final PCB design submission"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 3.1 – PCB Prototype", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 4 - Product Validation", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Value Engineering", "Mold flow Analysis", "Mold Feasibility", "DFM"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 5 – Manufacturing Readiness, Vendor Development & Sourcing", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Vendor development", "Tool development", "Batch production", "Component Sourcing"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Additional Phase 6 - Product Strategy, 360 Research Architecture", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Online & Offline survey", "Client study", "E-commerce study", "Area of opportunities as per survey", "Geographic study", "CMF study", "Threshold"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 7 - Packaging Development", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Packaging design development ", "Product placement and protection approach", "Packaging graphics & product communication", "Material & finish selection", "Packaging refinement & finalisation"], "deliverables": "-"}], "enabled": true, "timeline": "7-8 Weeks from Commencement of Project.", "is_custom": false, "outOfScope": ["Mass production tooling, mold making, and tool fabrication costs", "Regulatory certifications (BIS, EMC, FCC, CE) — quoted separately", "IP filings, design registration government fees, and trademark prosecution", "Post-launch warranty support beyond 30 days from handover"], "productName": "Extension Board Development", "validityNote": "This document is valid for 25 days from the date of issue.", "paymentSummary": ["50% Advance, 30% against Phase 1 and 20% against Project handover.", "Cost of all Prototyping is extra as per applicable.", "Quote is inclusive of all taxes.", "Any additions or changes to the Scope of Work (SOW) after finalizing the design or beyond three iterations will incur additional charges as applicable."], "successMetrics": [{"metric": "Design freeze achieved within Phase 1 timeline", "target": "4 weeks from kick-off"}, {"metric": "CAD files reviewed and signed off by tooling partner", "target": "≥ 1 vendor sign-off"}, {"metric": "Prototype passes agreed-upon test plan", "target": "≥ 90% pass rate"}, {"metric": "Final BOM cost variance vs. quoted target", "target": "≤ 5% deviation"}], "bankDetailsNote": "See \"Project Investment & Banking\" page for full wire transfer details.", "deliverablesNote": "As per above mentioned."}, {"id": "pkg_u0zq43k", "note": "", "label": "Growth Package", "phases": [{"inr": 495000, "name": "Phase 1 - Industrial Design + CMF with Schematics", "weeks": "4", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Kick off meeting & brief discussion", "Brainstorming & Ideation on schematic", "Client review & refinement of schematic", "Brainstorming & Concept Ideation for design", "Internal review & refinement of Design", "Concept 3D models", "Concept Renders", "ID presentation", "Client review & ID Refinement", "Final Presentation"], "deliverables": "1) Design presentation with 3 concept designs.\n2) 3 CMF combinations for selected concept."}, {"inr": "Included", "name": "Phase 1.1 – Alpha Prototype", "weeks": "Included", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "One Visual prototype of one selected concept."}, {"inr": 299000, "name": "Phase 2 - Product Engineering & Prototyping", "weeks": "4", "enabled": true, "activities": ["3D CAD models", "Review, update CAD files", "Engineering review & Updated CAD files", "File submission for prototyping/mold maker''s review", "Updated CAD files based on prototype/mold maker''s feedback", "Internal review & Engineering refinement", "Value Engineering", "Final submission"], "deliverables": "1) Engineering 3D CAD file of one selected concept''s components & Assembly based on final prototype. (Step or Parasolid)"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 2.1 - 2D CAD Drawings", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "As per Actuals", "name": "Phase 2.2 – Beta Prototype", "weeks": "As per Actuals", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "1) Functional/Near real Prototype as per approved materials."}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 3 - Electrical & Electronics Development", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Identify the components", "PCB architecture", "PCB design", "Review & refinements", "Final PCB design submission"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 3.1 – PCB Prototype", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 4 - Product Validation", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Value Engineering", "Mold flow Analysis", "Mold Feasibility", "DFM"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 5 – Manufacturing Readiness, Vendor Development & Sourcing", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Vendor development", "Tool development", "Batch production", "Component Sourcing"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Additional Phase 6 - Product Strategy, 360 Research Architecture", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Online & Offline survey", "Client study", "E-commerce study", "Area of opportunities as per survey", "Geographic study", "CMF study", "Threshold"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 7 - Packaging Development", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Packaging design development ", "Product placement and protection approach", "Packaging graphics & product communication", "Material & finish selection", "Packaging refinement & finalisation"], "deliverables": "-"}], "enabled": true, "timeline": "7-8 Weeks from Commencement of Project.", "is_custom": false, "outOfScope": ["Mass production tooling, mold making, and tool fabrication costs", "Regulatory certifications (BIS, EMC, FCC, CE) — quoted separately", "IP filings, design registration government fees, and trademark prosecution", "Post-launch warranty support beyond 30 days from handover"], "productName": "Extension Board Development", "validityNote": "This document is valid for 25 days from the date of issue.", "paymentSummary": ["50% Advance, 30% against Phase 1 and 20% against Project handover.", "Cost of all Prototyping is extra as per applicable.", "Quote is inclusive of all taxes.", "Any additions or changes to the Scope of Work (SOW) after finalizing the design or beyond three iterations will incur additional charges as applicable."], "successMetrics": [{"metric": "Design freeze achieved within Phase 1 timeline", "target": "4 weeks from kick-off"}, {"metric": "CAD files reviewed and signed off by tooling partner", "target": "≥ 1 vendor sign-off"}, {"metric": "Prototype passes agreed-upon test plan", "target": "≥ 90% pass rate"}, {"metric": "Final BOM cost variance vs. quoted target", "target": "≤ 5% deviation"}], "bankDetailsNote": "See \"Project Investment & Banking\" page for full wire transfer details.", "deliverablesNote": "As per above mentioned."}, {"id": "pkg_6tvvyrk", "note": "", "label": "Flagship Package", "phases": [{"inr": 594000, "name": "Phase 1 - Industrial Design + CMF with Schematics", "weeks": "6", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Kick off meeting & brief discussion", "Brainstorming & Ideation on schematic", "Client review & refinement of schematic", "Brainstorming & Concept Ideation for design", "Internal review & refinement of Design", "Concept 3D models", "Concept Renders", "ID presentation", "Client review & ID Refinement", "Final Presentation"], "deliverables": "1) Design presentation with 4 concept designs.\n2) 3 CMF combinations for selected concept."}, {"inr": "Included", "name": "Phase 1.1 – Alpha Prototype", "weeks": "Included", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "Visual prototype of all 4 concepts with one selected CMF option."}, {"inr": 385000, "name": "Phase 2 - Product Engineering & Prototyping", "weeks": "5", "enabled": true, "activities": ["3D CAD models", "Review, update CAD files", "Engineering review & Updated CAD files", "File submission for prototyping/mold maker''s review", "Updated CAD files based on prototype/mold maker''s feedback", "Internal review & Engineering refinement", "Value Engineering", "Final submission"], "deliverables": "1) Engineering 3D CAD file of one selected concept''s components & Assembly based on final prototype. (Step or Parasolid)"}, {"inr": "Included", "name": "Phase 2.1 - 2D CAD Drawings", "weeks": "Included", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "1) 2D drawings of selected concept. (In IUOVA''s drawing format)"}, {"inr": "As per Actuals", "name": "Phase 2.2 – Beta Prototype", "weeks": "As per Actuals", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "1) Functional/Near real Prototype as per approved materials."}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 3 - Electrical & Electronics Development", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Identify the components", "PCB architecture", "PCB design", "Review & refinements", "Final PCB design submission"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Phase 3.1 – PCB Prototype", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": [], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": 200000, "name": "Phase 4 - Product Validation", "weeks": "3", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Value Engineering", "Mold flow Analysis", "Mold Feasibility", "DFM"], "deliverables": "1) One report of Mould Flow Analysis (2 Iterations).\n2) One Mold feasibility report."}, {"inr": 200000, "name": "Phase 5 – Manufacturing Readiness, Vendor Development & Sourcing", "weeks": "3", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Vendor development", "Tool development", "Batch production", "Component Sourcing"], "deliverables": "1) Vendor Development for material sourcing, costing, & tooling."}, {"inr": "-", "name": "Additional Phase 6 - Product Strategy, 360 Research Architecture", "weeks": "-", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Online & Offline survey", "Client study", "E-commerce study", "Area of opportunities as per survey", "Geographic study", "CMF study", "Threshold"], "deliverables": "-"}, {"inr": 158000, "name": "Phase 7 - Packaging Development", "weeks": "2", "enabled": true, "activities": ["Packaging design development ", "Product placement and protection approach", "Packaging graphics & product communication", "Material & finish selection", "Packaging refinement & finalisation"], "deliverables": "1) Final packaging design\n2) 3D packaging visualisation using existing product CAD\n3) Packaging specification sheet (material, finish & dimensions)\n4) Final vendor handover files"}], "enabled": true, "timeline": "18-19 Weeks from Commencement of Project.", "is_custom": false, "outOfScope": ["Mass production tooling, mold making, and tool fabrication costs", "Regulatory certifications (BIS, EMC, FCC, CE) — quote